{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview","id":1516465,"title":"Rage-Dice - W5 Preview","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-28T09:06:29-07:00","id":1516465,"title":"Rage-Dice - W5 Preview","content":"<div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1493\" height=\"951\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/FvYDDuP.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/FvYDDuP.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/FvYDDuP.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"744\" height=\"955\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/royLNmQ.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/royLNmQ.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/royLNmQ.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> My thoughts:<ul><li>WP-damage for any Rage-gain over 5... every character needs WP 4 at least...</li> <li>&quot;Brutal outcome&quot;... okay, that goes way too far in my opinion...</li> <li>So Rage-checks are... nothing happens or one less Rage... that's weird... so using a Gift makes you somehow less angry...? They say it doesn't represent that but it does with how Rage Dice work, so that's a bit weird.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T09:59:44-07:00","id":1516474,"title":"","content":"Can you even play a viable character that is actually a Werewolf without at least 7 Willpower? I swear every single mechanic saps from Willpower to the point of stupidity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T10:02:43-07:00","id":1516476,"title":"","content":"This is just getting dull and predictable. They're even trying to force emulation of generic werewolf movies by making Garou howl nightly at the moon in order to recover from Losing the Wolf, which happens in <i>every</i> frenzy, according to the past previews. In other words, the expected outcome of staying in Crinos is losing the ability to shapeshift with 100% certainty. The incentives are getting awfully perverse for a werewolf game, unless it's the &quot;chain yourself up in the basement&quot; style of werewolf game.<br /> <br /> W:tA wasn't supposed to be a generic werewolf flick. It was supposed to be a new thing, its own, with more powerful and in some ways less troubled werewolves than what was the par for the course at the time. W5 is working hard to undo this distinctiveness, as well as just copy over Vampire mechanics, in this case Hunger and messy results. And then it goes so far as to injure characters from accumulating &quot;too much&quot; Rage.<br /> <br /> Is this really supposed to be better than just letting temporary Rage rise above permanent more often? Or giving bonus dice to Rage rolls while in Crinos? If you wanted characters that exploded from too many successes on dice rolls, well, you already had that in the earlier iterations of the rules. Just have them roll Rage instead of some other dice pools. Staying in Crinos becomes a different kind of show of self-control, and still allows for klaive use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T10:11:46-07:00","id":1516477,"title":"","content":"Also, re-reading it again, this bit from the side-bar is just so weird...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Likewise, a Storyteller should be mindful of players attempting to game the system by using Gifts or other abilities for the sake of dumping Rage. Spirits tend to frown on such abuse and recklessly calling upon them to perfrom Gifts is sure to have consequences. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, maybe this is more an indication that the interplay of systems with Gifts calling for Rage-checks doesn't quite work instead of accusing players of &quot;meta-gaming&quot;. Rage-checks can potentially lower your Rage so why wouldn't a player make use of that...? If it makes narrative sense in some way why not...? It wasn't the ST or any player who came up with the idea of &quot;Using Gifts can lower your Rage&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T10:47:57-07:00","id":1516486,"title":"","content":"These mechanics seem.......kinda half-baked and put a lot of weight on the STs shoulders to 'fix' system interactions that function in odd or counterintuitive ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T10:51:44-07:00","id":1516488,"title":"","content":"Sooo, what is the actual disadvantage of losing the wolf? Because from where I'm looking at it, there seems to be very little benefit to using your garou powers over just relying on basic human skills.<br /> <br /> Also, the Rite-like stuff is bizarre. A solemn retelling of a past event should not make you Rage angry. Heck, given the example of a soccer match, does this mean a garou can frenzy during church service? XD<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, I feel having the max Rage number be 5 is a massive issue in terms of balance. If we ignore the Rage dice, the whole point of Rage is that it is fluid and ever-moving. But 5 makes each use or loss far too punishing, there is a reason it went up to 10 in previous editions. Losing the wolf should be something that is hard to do, not the result of a single fight OR taking crinos.<br /> <br /> As Saur Ops above said, they are treating being garou as something akin to movie werewolves and not the born warriors of Gaia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 06-28-2023, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T11:02:21-07:00","id":1516490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516488#post1516488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooo, what is the actual disadvantage of losing the wolf? Because from where I'm looking at it, there seems to be very little benefit to using your garou powers over just relying on basic human skills.<br /> <br /> Also, the Rite-like stuff is bizarre. A solemn retelling of a past event should not make you Rage angry. Heck, given the example of a soccer match, does this mean a garou can frenzy during church service? XD<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The deal with &quot;Losing the Wolf&quot; seems to be: You can't do anything that requires a Rage-check (like shifting into anything besides Lupus and Homid, using Gifts and Rites or regenerating). So any mechanic that calls for that is inaccessible to your character plus you have to wait till the night to howl at the moon (or use a specific Ritual). Especially with the Ritual I don't get why the side-bar complains about players &quot;gaming the system&quot;... I mean, that's how it's designed. You're supposed to constantly worry about not getting too close to Rage 0 or having too much Rage (because of potential WP-damage and Brutal Outcomes on rolls). All of this is designed to make you micro-manage all potential ways to deal with your Rage-track!<br /> <br /> With the Rites-stuff... so the game really is penalizing you for doing Garou-related stuff. Because getting involved in those traditions immediately raises your Rage. And I guess the way it's phrased doing a retelling of a past grievance, like say a battle a Sept has lost in the past, wouldn't just raise your character's Rage but everybody who listens since you could technically count it as something like a provocation or humiliation.<br /> <br /> Also, this should apply to seeing a Touchstone harmed as well, shouldn't it? So, if your character sees one of their Touchstones harmed their Rage gets raised, they have to do a Frenzy check <i>and</i> they have to do a Harano-check...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T11:04:22-07:00","id":1516494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516488#post1516488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooo, what is the actual disadvantage of losing the wolf? Because from where I'm looking at it, there seems to be very little benefit to using your garou powers over just relying on basic human skills.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Losing the wolf means you can\u2019t use any powers from what I can tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T11:10:15-07:00","id":1516496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516494#post1516494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Losing the wolf means you can\u2019t use any powers from what I can tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is funny since they look like they are doing everything they can for you to <i>not</i> use anything Werewolf related.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T11:14:26-07:00","id":1516497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516494#post1516494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Losing the wolf means you can\u2019t use any powers from what I can tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 'powers' so far seem like something you could do without.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah, the whole point of having Rage being in a constant flux is trying to balance it. It isn't like players are activating the gifts for -nothing.-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T11:30:06-07:00","id":1516499,"title":"","content":"Oh and let's consider this paradox: Because of the way it's set up one of the best ways to lower your Rage quickly is shifting into Crinos. After all, you need to do two Rage-checks (so it's a potential -2 Rage). Not only that... If you attempt to shift into Crinos with less than Rage 3, two bad Rage-checks will immediately drop you out of Crinos again because two failed Rage-checks with Rage 1 or 2 means you &quot;lost the wolf&quot;/dropped to Rage 0. So it isn't just the WP-cost and Frenzy-risk that makes you avoid Crinos, the lack of Rage plus potential failed Rage-checks also disincentivize shifting into Crinos!<br /> <br /> At the same time having more than Rage 2 means all rolls are potentially set up for &quot;Brutal Outcomes&quot; (two or more 1s/2s on your Rage-dice) which means whatever you wanted to do fails - unless it's for the sake of a violent outcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T11:35:51-07:00","id":1516501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516499#post1516499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh and let's consider this paradox: Because of the way it's set up one of the best ways to lower your Rage quickly is shifting into Crinos. After all, you need to do two Rage-checks (so it's a potential -2 Rage). Not only that... If you attempt to shift into Crinos with less than Rage 3, two bad Rage-checks will immediately drop you out of Crinos again because two failed Rage-checks with Rage 1 or 2 means you &quot;lost the wolf&quot;/dropped to Rage 0. So it isn't just the WP-cost and Frenzy-risk that makes you avoid Crinos, the lack of Rage plus potential failed Rage-checks also disincentivize shifting into Crinos!<br /> <br /> At the same time having more than Rage 2 means all rolls are potentially set up for &quot;Brutal Outcomes&quot; (two or more 1s/2s on your Rage-dice) which means whatever you wanted to do fails - unless it's for the sake of a violent outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>And THEN we add the archetypes presented in the tribe previews to it and the whole thing breaks. HOW can these garou manage anything like a normal life if they are constantly trying to NOT gain too much or too low Rage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T11:43:30-07:00","id":1516502,"title":"","content":"By 'spirits' we mean game designers and by consequences we mean punitive railroading.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-28-2023, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T11:46:02-07:00","id":1516504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516501#post1516501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And THEN we add the archetypes presented in the tribe previews to it and the whole thing breaks. HOW can these garou manage anything like a normal life if they are constantly trying to NOT gain too much or too low Rage?</div> </div> </div> </div>And the more I think about the angrier I get about the sidebar then because it's probably something they saw in the playtests. And it's a reaction to that. But the thing this sidebar is complaining about is incentivized by the system they wrote! Of course, players start to meta-game the Rage-track: There are punishments awaiting players on both ends (&quot;Losing the wolf&quot; on one end, &quot;Brutal Outcomes&quot; and WP-damage on the other).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T11:52:31-07:00","id":1516505,"title":"","content":"Honestly, this is how I see the basic systems savvy game going; Everyone intentionally loses the wolf and then spends the session focusing on mechanics that don't punish them or suck up willpower.<br /> <br /> Given how this game works, shifting, Gifts, umbra etc. are not worth the Rage dice cost. And since so much of the fluff focus is on stuff outside the umbra, you can get far by just being in homid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T11:57:16-07:00","id":1516506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516505#post1516505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, this is how I see the basic systems savvy game going; Everyone intentionally loses the wolf and then spends the session focusing on mechanics that don't punish them or suck up willpower.<br /> <br /> Given how this game works, shifting, Gifts, umbra etc. are not worth the Rage dice cost. And since so much of the fluff focus is on stuff outside the umbra, you can get far by just being in homid.</div> </div> </div> </div>And to really underline it, you have the &quot;Brutal Outcomes&quot; with Rage-Dice. The whole idea of this Rage-system seems to be this: &quot;If you don't roleplay your Garou-character like they're already in Frenzy all the time, you're in trouble... and if things get really bad, you have to do a Frenzy-check with what little WP your character has left. And of course, we as game-designers give the ST permission to take over playing your character once they enter Frenzy in order to make sure you're playing this game <i>the right way</i>!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T12:24:21-07:00","id":1516509,"title":"","content":"Why would anyone ever play a Glass Walker with these rules? The entire system seems hell-bent on sucking every last point of willpower from players, brutal results cause large amounts of destruction, the game and setting really push a street level closeness to humanity (and by extension their technology), and the tribal ban hurts willpower recovery if you break complex things. Break an antagonists gun? Get punished. Sit on your cellphone the wrong way or drop it and Crack the screen? Get punished.<br /> <br /> This is less a game about raging against the state of the world and more about simple anger management. Being a werewolf just sucks massively in this game, where is the cool upside? Where is the fun?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","user":"Lunar Falcon","date":". 06-28-2023, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T12:34:25-07:00","id":1516511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516509#post1516509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would anyone ever play a Glass Walker with these rules? The entire system seems hell-bent on sucking every last point of willpower from players, brutal results cause large amounts of destruction, the game and setting really push a street level closeness to humanity (and by extension their technology), and the tribal ban hurts willpower recovery if you break complex things. Break an antagonists gun? Get punished. Sit on your cellphone the wrong way or drop it and Crack the screen? Get punished.<br /> <br /> This is less a game about raging against the state of the world and more about simple anger management. Being a werewolf just sucks massively in this game, where is the cool upside? Where is the fun?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're forgetting that any Rite, Tribe- and Auspice-related activity that gets you &quot;psyched up&quot; increases the character's Rage as well. In the case of Glass Walkers building/repairing anything technology related would qualify, I think (the example they offer even is a &quot;<i>solemn </i>retelling of past grievances&quot; and somehow that already qualifies as getting the character &quot;psyched up&quot;), so you need to add that to the list of things you get punished for... lol<br /> <br /> They really did end up creating a system for W5 that is all about telling players that being a Garou sucks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T12:37:51-07:00","id":1516512,"title":"","content":"It seems to have similar issues as the v5 hunger system in that as experiance with it builds up. You're eventuallu decentivised from engaging with mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T15:02:12-07:00","id":1516529,"title":"","content":"I'm just baffled at who's the audience for this. I get that Paradox is probably just hoping to sell a bunch of sight-unseen copies to V5 fans, but I can't imagine they're going to be happy with the purchase after the fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T15:17:56-07:00","id":1516533,"title":"","content":"I just realized something... sigh... This really is just gonna be as bad as H5 yet again, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Consider this... The Rage Dice section begins:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For each point of Rage possessed by a character, one Rage die replaces one of the regular dice when assembling dice pools. </div> </div> </div>That's all you get here and it's repeated again in the summary. But... the way this is written would expect you replace die with Rage dice for <i>every roll</i> in the game. So how would a WP-test interact with a Brutal Outcome...? After all, that's what this suggests you should do in this game. In V5 Willpower-tests are listed as an exception for Hunger but here... they aren't. This is supposed to be like Hunger but clearly, this write-up has overlooked a few... details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T15:48:10-07:00","id":1516536,"title":"","content":"I generally don't comment in those topics but I want to know if someone else laughed to &quot;...wether that's a nearly diceless chronicle of in-character intrigue against the crumbling remains of the Garou Nation...&quot;<br /> <br /> lol they really hate the past editions of this reimagining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T16:02:33-07:00","id":1516541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516529#post1516529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just baffled at who's the audience for this. I get that Paradox is probably just hoping to sell a bunch of sight-unseen copies to V5 fans, but I can't imagine they're going to be happy with the purchase after the fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Video games and movies. They don\u2019t make books for players, they make it so when they license it to someone they can hand over the book and go \u201cHere, do this\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T16:20:56-07:00","id":1516549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516541#post1516541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Video games and movies. They don\u2019t make books for players, they make it so when they license it to someone they can hand over the book and go \u201cHere, do this\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes even less sense though. How would a movie or video game about WTA be any fun if it went out of its way to disincentivise actually being a werewolf like this game does?<br /> <br /> The creators, knowingly or not, appear to have made a game about angst and being miserable, rather than anything compelling or fun to play. From what I've seen repeated about the playtesting for this edition people really avoid using crinos at all costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T16:31:42-07:00","id":1516551,"title":"","content":"Imagine if in the 90s you'd been handed a really, really bad DC or Marvel comic. It's the worst reimagining you can imagine. It's not really FOR anyone, it's kind of terrible, and it's rude to the writers of the old version too. It seems to go out of its way to mock the idea of being a superhero, and makes being a superhero kind of impossible too.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who is this for?&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh they want to license the comics to make movies and video games! Those are where the money's at.&quot;<br /> &quot;Ah. I see. But how will those movies and games compete with ones based on IPs people like?&quot;<br /> &quot;...&quot;<br /> &quot;And why would I risk my money investing in an IP with poor sales, hell, maybe an IP I used to like but has recently gotten much worse.&quot;<br /> &quot;It may not have been a GOOD plan.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T16:50:05-07:00","id":1516552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516549#post1516549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That makes even less sense though. How would a movie or video game about WTA be any fun if it went out of its way to disincentivise actually being a werewolf like this game does?<br /> <br /> The creators, knowingly or not, appear to have made a game about angst and being miserable, rather than anything compelling or fun to play. From what I've seen repeated about the playtesting for this edition people really avoid using crinos at all costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, maybe a drama about be cursed be something that you don't like, werewolf curse in this case, but in the end you do friends or even a lover that give you a reason to fight using you powers, but you refuse to use the Crinos because you can have the powers, but you aren't the beast you're the man, what means you use the Glabro that in this context is more man than beast. Something like Twilight + scenes of action from teen series. Yes I thought seriously about that and I can think someone doing a series with this ideia and selling in streaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T16:57:59-07:00","id":1516554,"title":"","content":"But why not just make your own Werewolf property? If W5's devs plan to make bank off of licensing, I'm guessing they plan for the license to cost $$$, but I can't see anyone paying anything significant to license WTA right now. W20 featured a broad, &quot;CW-able&quot; setting which you could turn into a TV show akin to Vampire Diaries, which I thankfully know way too much about because of an excellent Jenny Nicholson video. CW shows are full of bombastic, stupid, over the top supernatural and superhero settings with way too much going on, way too much angst and drama, and Fera + a huge spirit world + endless weird monsters which look like humans + prosthetics or some light CG is great for them.<br /> <br /> Instead we have a much smaller, much less ambitious, much more anaemic and *sad* version of Werewolf. One where the writers and characters seem to be embarrassed to be Werewolves, even. How do you market that to consumers? More importantly, how do you market it to a TV, film or game company?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T18:03:47-07:00","id":1516566,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I get that Paradox wants video games and movies and streaming TV shows... but you don't get those with shovelware editions of a RPG.<br /> <br /> Video games? You don't have a Storyteller in a video game. Game play loops that require a ST/GM/etc. to function at all? Those don't translate to video games play loops because computers can't parse things like the Rage Economy sidebar. Bloodlines 1's Humanity and Masquerade tracks are, at least in the base version of the game, pointless. Players absolutely figured out how to game them such that you can be a near sociopathic individual and still have Humanity 10 by doing some sidequests, and you can regain more Masquerade points then you'd ever lose unless you're actively trying to lose them (or playing a Nosferatu and don't figure out some of the stealth paths to plot locations). You could strip Humanity and Masquerade points from Bloodlines and lose nothing to the game play loop.<br /> <br /> &quot;This only works if a human is sitting there making sure you don't game it,&quot; is basically the same as, &quot;at best, this isn't going to matter to playing a video game.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T18:36:49-07:00","id":1516576,"title":"","content":"Furthermore, why would paradox absolutly want a new edition of the games? When the project of the world of darkness online was announced, no one was asking for a new edition.<br /> <br /> Same for the mess that was Earthblood, a werewolf game released long before any release date for W5 was announced, same for wraith afterlife.<br /> <br /> I've heard the argument that it is to base the video games mechanics on a set ground, which would be V5, which doesn't stand as an explaination since the biggest project, Bloodlines 2, doesn't use V5, having both a blood point meter and disciplines for thin blood...<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bIS it to revive the fanbase in order to ensure sales? That's no explaination either, since ironically, many were introduced to the ttrpg after playing bloodlines.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T18:51:17-07:00","id":1516579,"title":"","content":"I can see now why playtesters said nobody wanted to use Crinos. Wish they had made a werewolf game where you wanted to be a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T19:03:08-07:00","id":1516583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516554#post1516554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why not just make your own Werewolf property? If W5's devs plan to make bank off of licensing, I'm guessing they plan for the license to cost $$$, but I can't see anyone paying anything significant to license WTA right now. W20 featured a broad, &quot;CW-able&quot; setting which you could turn into a TV show akin to Vampire Diaries, which I thankfully know way too much about because of an excellent Jenny Nicholson video. CW shows are full of bombastic, stupid, over the top supernatural and superhero settings with way too much going on, way too much angst and drama, and Fera + a huge spirit world + endless weird monsters which look like humans + prosthetics or some light CG is great for them.<br /> <br /> Instead we have a much smaller, much less ambitious, much more anaemic and *sad* version of Werewolf. One where the writers and characters seem to be embarrassed to be Werewolves, even. How do you market that to consumers? More importantly, how do you market it to a TV, film or game company?</div> </div> </div> </div>Crinos, spirit worlds, enemies with deformed forms, all of these are expensive, it's much more attractive for investors if you make something cheaper that doesn't require a lot of resources or prowess to make, Crinos and Hipos would require a lot of CG to work and it's very easy to to get rough, so limit to Glabro which only requires makeup; complex spirit worlds would also require CG so the idea is to limit their use so when necessary you can invest in scenes with good figuration in key parts of the story, it can look cool and it's not as expensive as creating an effect; another option would be to make the scenes in the umbra in animation; as for the enemies and other shapeshifters, they must want something like supernatural, put teeth, contact lenses, CG in the eyes, and bigger nails, nothing much big and the biggest differentiation would be in mental powers that don't require special effects or if they do it's a small thing. As a fan this may seem off-putting, but from an investor's point of view this seems more attractive than a more expensive series. In the case of games, WOD already had games, but none expressive. So... these elements could be an attempt at that, but it could also be something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T19:28:59-07:00","id":1516591,"title":"","content":"Once again that is putting the cart before the horse. You need to have a compelling base product, lore, and a decently sized audience with enough buy in to try to sell additional products and spin offs to. This new edition has neither a compelling base game, fun system, or buy in from existing fans.<br /> <br /> It is actively doing its damndest to drive away the devoted players who had significant investment in prior editions. This watered down version that is openly antagonistic to earlier players seemingly has nothing to offer that we have seen thus far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T20:19:58-07:00","id":1516603,"title":"","content":"I have to disagree on a few things here; First of all both Heart of the Forest and Earthblood used some version of the W5 setting. What with Earthblood crinos being a battle ender and Heart of the Forest treating the Fenrir as semi-bad guys.<br /> <br /> But more than that, if they wanted to make W5 into shows or games (especially GAMES since it is paradox we are talking about), they would have dropped the 'protect the Earth' aspect entirely.<br /> <br /> See, the reason Bloodlines and most VtM games are easy to get into for non-fans is that the core of the vampire stays mostly the same. You are an undead creature that feeds on blood, the rest can be learned later.<br /> <br /> But in terms of successful werewolf games, being a werewolf is something you acquire on your own if you want to and often the werewolf isn't even the main point. Bloodborne is mostly about werewolves at the start but turns into a cosmic horror story. Skyrim and World of Warcraft have a werewolf plot IF you want to engage with it.<br /> <br /> (Also, you'll notice only one of those games is even fully about werewolves, the rest just have an additional werewolf flavour.)<br /> <br /> Most WtA games start with the state of the planet and so far that has clearly been a deterrent because it takes away from the cursed fantasy of being a werewolf. Vampire can have its primogens and camarillas, because the core of a vampire has not changed. But even W5 starts with 'the Earth is doomed, the apocalypse is here, you are the chosen warrior of Gaia', which is not a cursed being trying to find balance.<br /> <br /> Another thing, from my experience, most people wanting to play werewolves in videogames generally want the werewolf-form to last LONGER. Not be a short burst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T23:45:25-07:00","id":1516614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516603#post1516603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to disagree on a few things here; First of all both Heart of the Forest and Earthblood used some version of the W5 setting. What with Earthblood crinos being a battle ender</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard disagree on Earthblood, I played and finished Earthblood through combat aka Crinos as Stealth was pointles and slower.<br /> The only exception being the prison section since I wanted to immerse myself to story.<br /> In the end I was a silver wound regenerating murder machine that would make some Elder Werewolves ashamed of their combat ability.<br /> <br /> Plus setting elements, Fianna, Red Talons, Pentex still having subsidiaries and especially Crinos, really doesn't look like W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T23:56:51-07:00","id":1516616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516614#post1516614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hard disagree on Earthblood, I played and finished Earthblood through combat aka Crinos as Stealth was pointles and slower.<br /> The only exception being the prison section since I wanted to immerse myself to story.<br /> In the end I was a silver wound regenerating murder machine that would make some Elder Werewolves ashamed of their combat ability.<br /> <br /> Plus setting elements, Fianna, Red Talons, Pentex still having subsidiaries and especially Crinos, really doesn't look like W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh it isn't THIS w5, but it was a clearly a some version of W5 given how the crinos works. Remember that Fianna switched names VERY recently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T00:45:33-07:00","id":1516619,"title":"","content":"On a bit of an unrelated note, another curious thing about the latest update is that on the first page you get rules for &quot;Grappling&quot;. Now this is weird because last October this document called &quot;Expanded Mechanics&quot; <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/world-of-darkness-expanded-mechanics\" target=\"_blank\">was released</a> with this goal:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (If you have certain printings of Vampire: The Masquerade, you have a lot of this already, but we want to both make it available to everyone and to free up 20-ish pages of core book space for things that are specific to each of the games themselves. We can also update it as a living document, as new material or recurring edge cases merit it.) </div> </div> </div>And in this Expanded-Mechanics-document you have a section on &quot;Additional Conflict Options&quot; and one of them is &quot;Grappling&quot;. So originally the idea with the Expanded Mechanics document was that this corebook wouldn't have to include things like rules for &quot;Grappling&quot; because you're supposed to use this free pdf for that stuff instead. But clearly, it's still in the W5 corebook (and it is also still a copy-paste from the same bit in the V5 corebook - minus the rules for vampire-biting, of course) which, I guess, means that they abandoned the idea of this Expanded Mechanics pdf...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T00:59:30-07:00","id":1516620,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's being done purely for video game stuff. The origional setting was actually more video game friendly with its more combat friendly mechanics and larger richer setting to draw from.<br /> <br /> this is not to say they couldn't be doing it, it's just it would imply a level of stupidity I don't think is likely.<br /> <br /> Also they're seriously optermistic relying on their brand recognition at this stage if they're banking on video game spin offs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-29-2023, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T01:39:33-07:00","id":1516623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516603#post1516603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to disagree on a few things here; First of all both Heart of the Forest and Earthblood used some version of the W5 setting. What with Earthblood crinos being a battle ender and Heart of the Forest treating the Fenrir as semi-bad guys.<br /> <br /> But more than that, if they wanted to make W5 into shows or games (especially GAMES since it is paradox we are talking about), they would have dropped the 'protect the Earth' aspect entirely.<br /> <br /> See, the reason Bloodlines and most VtM games are easy to get into for non-fans is that the core of the vampire stays mostly the same. You are an undead creature that feeds on blood, the rest can be learned later.<br /> <br /> But in terms of successful werewolf games, being a werewolf is something you acquire on your own if you want to and often the werewolf isn't even the main point. Bloodborne is mostly about werewolves at the start but turns into a cosmic horror story. Skyrim and World of Warcraft have a werewolf plot IF you want to engage with it.<br /> <br /> (Also, you'll notice only one of those games is even fully about werewolves, the rest just have an additional werewolf flavour.)<br /> <br /> Most WtA games start with the state of the planet and so far that has clearly been a deterrent because it takes away from the cursed fantasy of being a werewolf. Vampire can have its primogens and camarillas, because the core of a vampire has not changed. But even W5 starts with 'the Earth is doomed, the apocalypse is here, you are the chosen warrior of Gaia', which is not a cursed being trying to find balance.<br /> <br /> Another thing, from my experience, most people wanting to play werewolves in videogames generally want the werewolf-form to last LONGER. Not be a short burst.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There's pretty much nothing in Earthblood that says &quot;W5 based&quot;. Crinos wasn't a battle ender, but a battle starter ironically.<br /> <br /> And frankly, the idea that wta isn't attractive to gamers (which is already a pretty dubious statement) due to it avoiding the cursed fantasy of werewolves is nonsense.<br /> <br /> The few games that have playable werewolves barely if ever touch that notion.<br /> <br /> The most notorious recent exemples, skyrim/elder scrolls online and wow have for the first the werewolves being a power without a real cost, and in wow, being a worgen is a curse for exactly a cinematic, after that you're going back to hero mode until a few quests later you gain full control over the worgen nature.<br /> <br /> <br /> You mentioned bloodlines staying close to the vampire fantasy. But it's the same for wta. The werewolf fantasy in pop culture is pretty simple: human become half beast and kills things. <br /> <br /> Wta only adds to that, the same way that vtm and therefore bloodlines add politics to the general vampire fantasy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T03:38:05-07:00","id":1516627,"title":"","content":"I'm really curious now how Kinfolk PC rules will compare (if they make any), more from a game design perspective than interest in playing. They need to somehow contrast mortals from Werewolves in a way that makes the latter the more attractive option, otherwise the premise of the game falls a bit flat. Ruleswise, if there is the option for giving Kinfolk Gnosis or Numina, it might be enough to just not bother with the whole wolf business.<br /> <br /> Edit: Right, I forgot Kinfolk isn't a thing as such. Replace with &quot;human allies&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 06-29-2023, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T04:12:36-07:00","id":1516629,"title":"","content":"Can I say, a little off topic, but tangentially related to the idea of making $$$ by licensing, rather than through book sales - I hate &quot;IP&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not a setting, not a world, not a lore, not a story, nor a game nor a book. It's just... IP.<br /> <br /> Intellectual Property.<br /> <br /> A possession. Something you can leverage and finance and sell and rent out and try to bank on. An investment.<br /> <br /> Obviously we live in a society where any successful piece of art, outside of fringe stuff like street art and hobbyists (and sometimes not even then!) is a commercial endeavor. That's a given. But when it becomes apparent that something beloved like Werewolf, Vampire, Mage etc. has been reduced to an &quot;IP&quot;, a problem child which needs to be poked and prodded until it can be profitable and 'Make It On The Big Screen' or 'Get A Vidya Game!' is just... sad. I make my living working in a hospital, I'm not an artist, and I write in my spare time as an amateur, a hobbyist. Still, were I a creative lead on a new edition of a beloved tabletop game, I'd want to make it as good as I possibly could. Make it a fun, balanced, interesting game, one which sells copies of its corebook. Merch, licensing, supplements, that all comes later.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately when a company buys an &quot;IP&quot; it wants to squeeze blood from the stone, and WoD has never been... that profitable. It's about as famous as TTRPG settings get without literally being D&amp;D, but I don't think anyone has ever gotten rich off of VTM, even at its height. It isn't a good investment. It's just a good game. I wish that were enough!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T04:45:23-07:00","id":1516633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516623#post1516623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mentioned bloodlines staying close to the vampire fantasy. But it's the same for wta. The werewolf fantasy in pop culture is pretty simple: human become half beast and kills things.<br /> <br /> Wta only adds to that, the same way that vtm and therefore bloodlines add politics to the general vampire fantasy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Human become half beast and kill things is the reason why WtA gets side-eyed. Because that is not what the game is about. For one, garou are born not made and breeding has a huge role in the game. Cue the furry comparisons.<br /> <br /> Second, most of the game is not really focused on turning into beast and killing things. While you do DO that, it is all framed under saving the Earth and most importantly fighting against technology and corporations. This makes people feel you are not REALLY playing anything as cool as a werewolf, but just furry captain planet.<br /> <br /> Third, you can play VtM without 90% of its lore. WtA relies on its lore heavily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T06:22:25-07:00","id":1516639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516633#post1516633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Human become half beast and kill things is the reason why WtA gets side-eyed. Because that is not what the game is about. For one, garou are born not made and breeding has a huge role in the game. Cue the furry comparisons.<br /> <br /> Second, most of the game is not really focused on turning into beast and killing things. While you do DO that, it is all framed under saving the Earth and most importantly fighting against technology and corporations. This makes people feel you are not REALLY playing anything as cool as a werewolf, but just furry captain planet.<br /> <br /> Third, you can play VtM without 90% of its lore. WtA relies on its lore heavily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well ... Not anymore, as far as we know about W5 Garou are not (necessarily) born, breeding has no role, and W5 seems predicated on making you play without relying heavily on the lore. <br /> <br /> The rest (saving the Earth and fighting against corporations) stays true, but it gets a grittier and splatter tone. <br /> <br /> It surely will be a different game in many of its elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T07:06:27-07:00","id":1516642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516639#post1516639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well ... Not anymore, as far as we know about W5 Garou are not (necessarily) born, breeding has no role, and W5 seems predicated on making you play without relying heavily on the lore.<br /> <br /> The rest (saving the Earth and fighting against corporations) stays true, but it gets a grittier and splatter tone.<br /> <br /> It surely will be a different game in many of its elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel they took out lot of the stuff that would have gone generally well, while keeping the biggest hurdle (save the world, warriors of Gaia.)<br /> <br /> I mean, a lot of my issues with the fluff can be really boiled down to treating saving the world as a MASSIVE burden and a bother since the garou now have jobs and clearly just want to do their own stuff. Remove the apocalypse and warriors of gaia and you might still end up with a very poor port of forsaken. But at least the port would reflect the freedom these garou have/want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T07:38:39-07:00","id":1516648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516633#post1516633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Third, you can play VtM without 90% of its lore. WtA relies on its lore heavily.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but the rich lore deep settings is half the appeal of wod games. Especially now they're rules light except when it comes to railroading. Dumbing down the clans was probably one of v5s worst decisions <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T08:06:20-07:00","id":1516652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516648#post1516648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True but the rich lore deep settings is half the appeal of wod games. Especially now they're rules light except when it comes to railroading. Dumbing down the clans was probably one of v5s worst decisions</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, just that unlike WtA, VtM can start with your basic vampire knowledge. While WtA requires you to learn a whole ass new culture with its terms, PLUS the Earth saving.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm not saying WtA is impossible to get into (sitting here in my Red Talon shirt next to a whole bookshelf of WtA book XD) Just that IF you want a werewolf experience akin to Howling or Blood and Chocolate, WtA is not that game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T13:35:06-07:00","id":1516685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516633#post1516633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Human become half beast and kill things is the reason why WtA gets side-eyed. Because that is not what the game is about. For one, garou are born not made and breeding has a huge role in the game. Cue the furry comparisons.</div> </div> </div> </div>again, I wonder where you get the idea that wta is side eyed. Or that the game isn't about becoming a beast and killing things.<br /> <br /> If anything, the lore of wta is what attract people. Just playing a random joe becoming a beast to kill a few people is not something that attracts audience on the middle to long run. Same for vtm. If it was just &quot;drink blood, hide from the sun&quot;, the setting would have never been that popular.<br /> <br /> One just has to look to the difference in popularity between masquerade and requiem to see that masquerade relies on it's lore massively.<br /> <br /> Requiem 1st ed showed that you can't just rely on the gimmicks of a supernatural creature to be a great game. And werewolf the forsaken showed the same in comparison to apocalypse. The dense lore of these games is a core component of their succes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Plus, I think you're exagerating the amount of lore needed to understand wta.<br /> <br /> &quot;You are werewolves, descendant of a warrior race bathed in an animistic world where you have to protect the soul of the world from the wyrm, the incarnation of everything wrong and corrupt&quot;<br /> <br /> How is that more dense than an explaination for vtm?<br /> <br /> &quot;You are vampires, cursed to drink the blood of mortals and avoid the sun, hiding from humans in under the rule of the masquerade, and facing treats from the endless conspirations of the elders of your race&quot;<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> I mean, how hard is that? I introduced more than a dozen players to the game in about as much words.<br /> <br /> We're talking about gaming audience, both ttrpg and video games. A paragraph of explaination is not hard.<br /> <br /> Plus you can play wta without learning anything about the garou culture. Play a group of exiled/young garou and you can never reference the garou nation, the impergium and so on without issue.<br /> <br /> &quot;<br /> Honestly, I'm not saying WtA is impossible to get into (sitting here in my Red Talon shirt next to a whole bookshelf of WtA book XD) Just that IF you want a werewolf experience akin to Howling or Blood and Chocolate, WtA is not that game.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> Excuse me, but that's really not a good argument. The same can be said about vtm, which by it's very lore forbid you from having the experience of, well, any vampire story, game or novel where you can actually walk under the sun for a start.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 06-29-2023, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T13:42:19-07:00","id":1516687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516685#post1516685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> again, I wonder where you get the idea that wta is side eyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simply from my own experiences and what I have seen/heard people say. Is it everyone? No, of course not. But I have seen the Furry Captain Planet mentality enough that it isn't just a few people.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As an example, these are opinions I found by just googling Furry Captain Planet Werewolf the apocalypse;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's a game with <i>werewolves</i> that isn't about <i>werewolves</i>\u200b&quot; - Gamepressure<br /> <br /> &quot;Move over, <i>Captain Planet</i>: <i>Werewolf the Apocalypse</i>: Earthblood ... environmentally-conscious hero with no shortage of <i>fur</i>, fangs, or talons.\u200b&quot; -Screen Rant<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i> \u2013 Earthblood Review. ... They're basically like <i>Captain Planet's</i> Planeteers, but instead of asking you to recycle\u200b&quot; -Well-played.com<br /> <br /> And these are JUST Earthblood reviews, which wasn't even as heavy on the stuff as the books are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 06-29-2023, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T14:12:18-07:00","id":1516690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516648#post1516648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True but the rich lore deep settings is half the appeal of wod games. Especially now they're rules light except when it comes to railroading. Dumbing down the clans was probably one of v5s worst decisions</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I never understood any sort of impulse to go away from the old canon in major ways with new editions of oWOD. Sure, they have their warts but there aren't many RPGs around that can stake a claim to such a trove of lore like oWOD. This should be utilized - not abandoned. And if the warts of this &quot;very 90s&quot;-ass writing make you wince - then the obvious decision there is to not pick up the IP. Wanting oWOD-games that still honor the old lore while also banishing all of the old stuff seems too much like an &quot;I want to have my cake and eat it too&quot;-type of move. And the obvious contradictions will create obvious problems... but here we are with H5 and W5 both trying to be new iterations of old stuff while wanting to have nothing to do with the old stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T15:27:50-07:00","id":1516699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516687#post1516687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Simply from my own experiences and what I have seen/heard people say. Is it everyone? No, of course not. But I have seen the Furry Captain Planet mentality enough that it isn't just a few people.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As an example, these are opinions I found by just googling Furry Captain Planet Werewolf the apocalypse;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's a game with <i>werewolves</i> that isn't about <i>werewolves</i>\u200b&quot; - Gamepressure<br /> <br /> &quot;Move over, <i>Captain Planet</i>: <i>Werewolf the Apocalypse</i>: Earthblood ... environmentally-conscious hero with no shortage of <i>fur</i>, fangs, or talons.\u200b&quot; -Screen Rant<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i> \u2013 Earthblood Review. ... They're basically like <i>Captain Planet's</i> Planeteers, but instead of asking you to recycle\u200b&quot; -Well-played.com<br /> <br /> And these are JUST Earthblood reviews, which wasn't even as heavy on the stuff as the books are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Again, how does the furry captain planet meme makes wta a side eyed ip? <br /> <br /> We had this conversation again and again with Leshet, bad actor at heat. The whole &quot;furry captain planet&quot; is a meme. It's not reprensentative on how the larger community of gamers sees it.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> And frankly, if you want to use reviews as arguments, don't use video game journalists as a source. They're notoriously bad at, well, anything. Their opinion is worthless.<br /> <br /> Especially when they are talking about earthblood, which lacks most of the worldbuilding of wta. It would be like talking about vtm based only on the game &quot;We eat blood&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T15:28:53-07:00","id":1516700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516690#post1516690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I never understood any sort of impulse to go away from the old canon in major ways with new editions of oWOD. Sure, they have their warts but there aren't many RPGs around that can stake a claim to such a trove of lore like oWOD. This should be utilized - not abandoned. And if the warts of this &quot;very 90s&quot;-ass writing make you wince - then the obvious decision there is to not pick up the IP. Wanting oWOD-games that still honor the old lore while also banishing all of the old stuff seems too much like an &quot;I want to have my cake and eat it too&quot;-type of move. And the obvious contradictions will create obvious problems... but here we are with H5 and W5 both trying to be new iterations of old stuff while wanting to have nothing to do with the old stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Brace yourself for Mage 5th. It will be glorious. In an apocalyptic sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T15:40:39-07:00","id":1516704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516699#post1516699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole &quot;furry captain planet&quot; is a meme. It's not reprensentative on how the larger community of gamers sees it.<br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Who... exactly do you think started that meme? It wasn't fans of the game going out and mocking it to try to sell it to the larger gamer community. It's a meme because that's its reputation in the wider gaming community; something very shallow readings of the text support because you need to actually get into the game to get into all that lore that fans love.<br /> <br /> You're also trying to compare the popularity of the cWoD to the 1e of the CofD... but you're forgetting that it took years for VtM to get that popular, and that was after it was into its second edition with lots of rules fixes and lots of time to build up lore while enjoying the benefits of a great economy where consumers were spending more freely than when VtR 1e came out. Popular also isn't the game as &quot;great.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T15:58:36-07:00","id":1516706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516699#post1516699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Again, how does the furry captain planet meme makes wta a side eyed ip?<br /> <br /> We had this conversation again and again with Leshet, bad actor at heat. The whole &quot;furry captain planet&quot; is a meme. It's not reprensentative on how the larger community of gamers sees it.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> And frankly, if you want to use reviews as arguments, don't use video game journalists as a source. They're notoriously bad at, well, anything. Their opinion is worthless.<br /> <br /> Especially when they are talking about earthblood, which lacks most of the worldbuilding of wta. It would be like talking about vtm based only on the game &quot;We eat blood&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Lashet prefers to make endless and extremely labored references to Game of Thrones more than anything else. If he mentions Ramsey Bolton, take a drink. If it's in reference to how he wishes that all Garou would die, take three drinks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T16:16:22-07:00","id":1516709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516704#post1516704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who... exactly do you think started that meme? It wasn't fans of the game going out and mocking it to try to sell it to the larger gamer community. It's a meme because that's its reputation in the wider gaming community; something very shallow readings of the text support because you need to actually get into the game to get into all that lore that fans love.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> to be fair it's pretty funny, especially when combined with Philosophy knife fights for mage and heroin junkie sex pest for vampire (my girlfriend also give me catholic space nazis for dark heresy and racist star trek for rogue trader) The problem is when some idiot mistakes the ribbing for reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T18:57:21-07:00","id":1516716,"title":"","content":"A problem i've seen with certain criticisms of wod5 is that sometimes people read a preview or a dev comment and extrapolate something the dev or preview never stated,or even downright put words in a dev's mouth, case in point this preview did not say every single Rite gives a werewolf Rage. and this Preview did not say the entire garou nation is entirely gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 06-29-2023, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T19:14:38-07:00","id":1516720,"title":"","content":"Care to cite something specific? Or just convincing people that aren't happy with the previews they're not missing out by not having to game with the people that love them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T19:18:35-07:00","id":1516722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516720#post1516720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Care to cite something specific? Or just convincing people that aren't happy with the previews they're not missing out by not having to game with the people that love them?</div> </div> </div> </div>holden shearer: <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/holden.shearer/posts/pfbid0gazVa86J8otz52dVLcRPEG7cVWm8TM14GsRsBtrGWFA1R2RunCQi2aQR5ZqzYd1el\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/holden.shea...i2aQR5ZqzYd1el</a><br /> he made a a lot statements here. not a single one became true.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T19:21:34-07:00","id":1516723,"title":"","content":"Specifically about V5 there's the idea that the Camarilla is unplayable being banded around in this forum. that's not true at all, you're encouraged to play a Camarilla vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T19:26:48-07:00","id":1516724,"title":"","content":"specifically about this preview,someone somewhere made a bad faith comment about how &quot;You can get rid of rage by killing a bug&quot; despite that making absolutely no sense whatsoever. Bugs are not sentient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T20:32:27-07:00","id":1516726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516722#post1516722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">holden shearer: <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/holden.shearer/posts/pfbid0gazVa86J8otz52dVLcRPEG7cVWm8TM14GsRsBtrGWFA1R2RunCQi2aQR5ZqzYd1el\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/holden.shea...i2aQR5ZqzYd1el</a><br /> he made a a lot statements here. not a single one became true.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that these things didn't become true doesn't prove that it was an unfair speculation from the previews at the time. For example, Martin specifically said he wanted to do a new book on the Rroma people. It didn't happen because Paradox got rid of Martin, but because anyone was misrepresenting the developer at the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516723#post1516723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically about V5 there's the idea that the Camarilla is unplayable being banded around in this forum. that's not true at all, you're encouraged to play a Camarilla vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody around here says the Camarilla is unplayable. They feel like they &quot;encouragement&quot; to play the Camarilla is hypocritical because the Camarilla was written to be unfun to play in V5's metaplot as it seems like the V5 developers (based plenty on their own words) want the primary PC Sect to be the Anarchs with the Camarilla returning to their original status as The Man for the PC Anarchs to rebel against.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516724#post1516724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...someone somewhere made a bad faith comment...</div> </div> </div> </div>You're currently being a someone, somewhere, on the Internet making a bad faith argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T20:49:18-07:00","id":1516728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516716#post1516716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and this Preview did not say the entire garou nation is entirely gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think when people say this, they're merely referring to what was said in the previews last October and what the W5 corebook says on page 15:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Garou Nation: A loose coalition of Garou tribes, ostensibly with common goals in service to Gaia; <b>the Garou Nation has sundered in the age of Apocalypse, and invoking it now can come across as idealistic or backward-looking\u200b</b> </div> </div> </div>(Emphasis mine)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T20:55:59-07:00","id":1516730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516726#post1516726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that these things didn't become true doesn't prove that it was an unfair speculation from the previews at the time. For example, Martin specifically said he wanted to do a new book on the Rroma people. It didn't happen because Paradox got rid of Martin, but because anyone was misrepresenting the developer at the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nobody around here says the Camarilla is unplayable. They feel like they &quot;encouragement&quot; to play the Camarilla is hypocritical because the Camarilla was written to be unfun to play in V5's metaplot as it seems like the V5 developers (based plenty on their own words) want the primary PC Sect to be the Anarchs with the Camarilla returning to their original status as The Man for the PC Anarchs to rebel against.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You're currently being a someone, somewhere, on the Internet making a bad faith argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit that I was In.bas faith because I got too emotionally invested. Wth the time to cool down,I can seer the difference between being angry while speculating and being Angry at something one knows for certain it will be on the game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T20:56:42-07:00","id":1516731,"title":"","content":"Me thinks rage dice have the same trouble as Hunger Dice, they are too intrusive and random in gameplay.<br /> <br /> People buying werewolf expect to be able to play as a furry war machine, not a monster with bipolar disorder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T21:52:41-07:00","id":1516732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516699#post1516699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Again, how does the furry captain planet meme makes wta a side eyed ip?<br /> <br /> We had this conversation again and again with Leshet, bad actor at heat. The whole &quot;furry captain planet&quot; is a meme. It's not reprensentative on how the larger community of gamers sees it.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> And frankly, if you want to use reviews as arguments, don't use video game journalists as a source. They're notoriously bad at, well, anything. Their opinion is worthless.<br /> <br /> Especially when they are talking about earthblood, which lacks most of the worldbuilding of wta. It would be like talking about vtm based only on the game &quot;We eat blood&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As Heavy Arms well put it, it is an oversimplification of the game that sadly IS the most common outside view of the game. That is also the reason I brought up the game reviews, because it doesn't matter if they are in the wrong, that their uniformed reaction to the very VERY simplified take on the setting still was &quot;lol, captain planet&quot; is enough to showcase how easily WtA can be sidelined as just Furry Captain Planet.<br /> <br /> It also applies to some of the W5 aspects. I have seen some takes that the new crinos is better &quot;because it feels more werewolf&quot; or &quot;you aren't playing mini golf in it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T23:06:22-07:00","id":1516735,"title":"","content":"Crinos mini-golf is surreal. It always ends in Garou tying the clubs around some dudes' heads and popping them off like a toothpaste cap after someone steps on the tube.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T01:14:28-07:00","id":1516740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516700#post1516700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brace yourself for Mage 5th. It will be glorious. In an apocalyptic sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, well, we know what JA thought the central conflict of MtA is about (for him it was about &quot;authoritarianism vs self-determination&quot;/Technocracy vs Traditions). But he no longer works there and WOD5E still doesn't have a lead-dev at the moment. Personally, my bet is that the development-part of the in-house WOD-team gets dissolved and the development of future WOD5E-books (both corebooks and supplements) is entirely given over to Renegade. But... who knows... I guess we'll see what will happen after the W5 corebook has been released.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T01:34:54-07:00","id":1516741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516720#post1516720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Care to cite something specific? Or just convincing people that aren't happy with the previews they're not missing out by not having to game with the people that love them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nicholas has all the reasons, there's a fair deal of discussions here where previews lead to extrapolation in the widest and most damagaging to the game possible sense, which are also usually assumed as consolidated facts (Imagery is less Crinos-centric means Paradox hates furries; &quot;Sustained stay in the Umbra causes damage&quot; means you will not be able to enter the Umbra without suffering damage; mange wolf with exposed ribs means devs are convinced wild wolves have this appearance; Rage mechanic, as well as Hunger mechanics, means you will not be able to use your powers; street level is the only possible way of playing; tracing is theft straightaway; the continued Achilli-bashing arguing he was actively trying to destroy a game he hates, based on 1999 comments on the Web etc etc)<br /> <br /> If we extend the discussion to V5, the tone is the same;<br /> <br /> Really, we could refer to the general tone of all the preview discussions; it's not bad faith, just extreme displeasure, and it's perfectly understandable as a social phenomena, but it's still grounded in an extreme depiction and doomish exageration of things we have seen; and it also comes with (again, understandable) tangible displeasure when someone is instead happy or at least positively curious of what is going on;<br /> <br /> If we go out of the forum, people bad-mouthing Wod5e with things bordering on defamation is really easy to find; also, every possible accusation against the Wod5e team, by a vocal part of the fanbase, has always been accepted as absolute truth, without a grain of doubt (from neonazism to racism etc etc);<br /> <br /> Again, it's the Internet; but let's not pretend everyone in discussions about Wod5e is sipping thea while arguing a la John Locke","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 06-30-2023, 04:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T01:46:03-07:00","id":1516742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516731#post1516731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People buying werewolf expect to be able to play as a furry war machine, not a monster with bipolar disorder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder what they'd do for mage (if they can wrap their head around it) Ego dice? Oh, you rolled 1's/10's time to brag about your new device.... Paradox dice? You just wanted to say hi and make a good impression when your hand you were waving suddenly became an octopus... <br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, 5th edition is all about the mentally ill crowd, because that's all us grownups playing make-pretend with dice nailed, really. Everything's a metaphor for neurodivergence. Can't say I'm amused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T01:46:12-07:00","id":1516743,"title":"","content":"I feel this is mostly people who have vague idea of what Werewolf is and who mostly learn from memes and internet conversations rather than actual books.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is rather frontloaded with a ton of lore and tools that you get out of the door. This can be a hurdle to starting your own game and needs a st willing to break down the setting, garou abilities and culture before starting.<br /> <br /> W5 has made an effort to simplify those things. However I feel it has approached this the wrong wqy as it's too invested in using the IP elements and making statements about how old werewolf was bad to stand on its own two legs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T02:13:12-07:00","id":1516744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516743#post1516743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel this is mostly people who have vague idea of what Werewolf is and who mostly learn from memes and internet conversations rather than actual books.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is rather frontloaded with a ton of lore and tools that you get out of the door. This can be a hurdle to starting your own game and needs a st willing to break down the setting, garou abilities and culture before starting.<br /> <br /> W5 has made an effort to simplify those things. However I feel it has approached this the wrong wqy as it's too invested in using the IP elements and making statements about how old werewolf was bad to stand on its own two legs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> I legit feel if they just lost the Nation and the Apocalypse or made them into stuff of legends things wouldn't be as annoyingly confusing.<br /> <br /> Though, we'd still deal with the issue of the fluff pushing for human contact and jobs and the Rage mechanics making such things very hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T02:22:30-07:00","id":1516745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516722#post1516722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> holden shearer: <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/holden.shearer/posts/pfbid0gazVa86J8otz52dVLcRPEG7cVWm8TM14GsRsBtrGWFA1R2RunCQi2aQR5ZqzYd1el\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/holden.shearer/posts/pfbid0gazVa86J8otz52dVLcRPEG7cVWm8TM14GsRsBtrGWFA1 R2RunCQi2aQR5ZqzYd1el</a><br /> he made a a lot statements here. not a single one became true.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Bloody hell, that's a lot of swing and misses. This reflects pretty badly on holden, I have a low opinion on Zak but he's pretty easy to bury on his own lack of merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-30-2023, 06:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T02:33:01-07:00","id":1516746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516723#post1516723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically about V5 there's the idea that the Camarilla is unplayable being banded around in this forum. that's not true at all, you're encouraged to play a Camarilla vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its soft pressure, certain setting modifications and the implicit assumptions about style of play. Sane thing with lupus.<br /> it should however be noted that Sabbat/metis/several tribes play is explicitly discouraged which reflects very badly on 5th ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T02:41:49-07:00","id":1516748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516744#post1516744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This.<br /> <br /> I legit feel if they just lost the Nation and the Apocalypse or made them into stuff of legends things wouldn't be as annoyingly confusing.<br /> <br /> Though, we'd still deal with the issue of the fluff pushing for human contact and jobs and the Rage mechanics making such things very hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could've gone the route of H5 I guess and retain the name WtA but it's a game about werewolves but you're not playing Garou and there are no Garou in the setting. But then you'd still have the comparisons with WtF. And the issue with H5 for me wasn't that it erased the Imbued and more stuff like its weird take on making hunter orgs secondary antagonists or how the book has no rules for creating your own supernatural antagonists. Similar to that, my issues are less about that it's different from the old WtA but in how the game presents itself.<br /> <br /> I guess it would unclutter the setting more if it had been as radical as H5 in its world building but the new ideas that are brought to the table here... I don't know. The focus on volatility and centering werewolves more on their human lives and contacts... For me it runs into a similar issue like H5 where I look at HtV and just like that more. And here the comparison to WtF 2E would lead to a similar result for me at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T02:51:36-07:00","id":1516749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516748#post1516748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They could've gone the route of H5 I guess and retain the name WtA but it's a game about werewolves but you're not playing Garou and there are no Garou in the setting. But then you'd still have the comparisons with WtF. And the issue with H5 for me wasn't that it erased the Imbued and more stuff like its weird take on making hunter orgs secondary antagonists or how the book has no rules for creating your own supernatural antagonists. Similar to that, my issues are less about that it's different from the old WtA but in how the game presents itself.<br /> <br /> I guess it would unclutter the setting more if it had been as radical as H5 in its world building but the new ideas that are brought to the table here... I don't know. The focus on volatility and centering werewolves more on their human lives and contacts... For me it runs into a similar issue like H5 where I look at HtV and just like that more. And here the comparison to WtF 2E would lead to a similar result for me at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>H5 kind of got away with that since origional reckoning wasn't that popular....and even then it didn't get away it becausw nobody liked the game. I suspect If W5 had tried the fan backlash would be apoplectic in scale and they'd have to deal with old fans shitting on the game until the end of time....moreso than currently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-30-2023, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T03:02:59-07:00","id":1516750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516749#post1516749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> H5 kind of got away with that since origional reckoning wasn't that popular....and even then it didn't get away it becausw nobody liked the game. I suspect If W5 had tried the fan backlash would be apoplectic in scale and they'd have to deal with old fans shitting on the game until the end of time....moreso than currently.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Although this also has led to some strange line development for WOD5E since now you have V5 that while making a lot of changes still wants to be recognized as a continuation, you have H5 that has completely ditched the legacy stuff and you have W5 while making a lot of changes still has some links to legacy stuff but explicitly doesn't want to be recognized as a continuation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T03:11:10-07:00","id":1516751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516742#post1516742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder what they'd do for mage (if they can wrap their head around it) Ego dice? Oh, you rolled 1's/10's time to brag about your new device.... Paradox dice? You just wanted to say hi and make a good impression when your hand you were waving suddenly became an octopus...<br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, 5th edition is all about the mentally ill crowd, because that's all us grownups playing make-pretend with dice nailed, really. Everything's a metaphor for neurodivergence. Can't say I'm amused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty likely-Paradox dice for messy crits, you'll have touchstones to stop you going into quiets. The Traditions if they exist will be archeotypes rather than organizations. Magic won't be very good anyway with the negatives of being a mage outstaking the positives by a considerable margin. Union play verboten. Low level street play only so no fighting dragons on the moons of neptune or trapping a onceborn in a riddle made of love-you're going to be using spells to pick a lock to a warehouse because you can't make rent. Huge chunks stolen from awakening. Thematically 'gritty' and 'street'.<br /> <br /> possible-union complete mystery. Massive emphasis on orphans. Loads of traditions missing or gone. Magic is so bad you're actually better pumping xp into conventional skills.<br /> <br /> Unlikely but looking at 5th in general....<br /> <br /> Everyone's basically an orphan but with a flavour (hermetic, druid, techo) 9mts destroyed and discredited. Union ascendant and pure evil bassically being the seers from awakening. Sphere system completely gone replaced with something more balanced but far more restrictive....possibly based of pillars.<br /> <br /> <br /> Plus they'll probably generate some controversy with anti vax or somesuch and become even more cowardly even if its just someone on twitter being an arse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-30-2023, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T03:17:09-07:00","id":1516752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516742#post1516742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder what they'd do for mage</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably they will be &quot;Mages' without magic maybe sorcery like abilites (or thechonology? Any sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic..) or alchemical solutions and when they use them it will trigger a paradox-dice with disasterous consequences... oh and the main focus will be it is how bad to be a Mage?<br /> ...so will be more logical to NOT use your &quot;powers&quot; just parlor tricks<br /> <br /> Wouldn't be surprised...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T04:31:50-07:00","id":1516757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516724#post1516724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">specifically about this preview,someone somewhere made a bad faith comment about how &quot;You can get rid of rage by killing a bug&quot; despite that making absolutely no sense whatsoever. Bugs are not sentient.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if you are referring to me because I made a comment in another thread where rules as written for crinos says you have to kill something each turn or check for frenzy. Do I think that squishing a bug each turn is a great interpretation of the rules? No, but gamers are notorious for finding loopholes and exploiting sloppy writing and mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T05:49:09-07:00","id":1516763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516748#post1516748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it would unclutter the setting more if it had been as radical as H5 in its world building but the new ideas that are brought to the table here... I don't know. The focus on volatility and centering werewolves more on their human lives and contacts... For me it runs into a similar issue like H5 where I look at HtV and just like that more. And here the comparison to WtF 2E would lead to a similar result for me at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, yeah, but if the people are just looking for a werewolf game about those things then it'd be at least clear on its intention.<br /> <br /> Though I truly wish they had taken time to make sure the fluff matches the crunch, which was a MASSIVE issue in WtA (see; every single NPC with a job and high Rage.) Or keep the fluff consistent on whether the werewolves can have mostly normal lives or do they have to live in the fringes. I showed the Rage Dice rules to a (non-WtA fan) buddy and he was baffled how the heck was the pc supposed to hold a job and still deal with Rage?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T07:31:36-07:00","id":1516772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516763#post1516763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, yeah, but if the people are just looking for a werewolf game about those things then it'd be at least clear on its intention.<br /> <br /> Though I truly wish they had taken time to make sure the fluff matches the crunch, which was a MASSIVE issue in WtA (see; every single NPC with a job and high Rage.) Or keep the fluff consistent on whether the werewolves can have mostly normal lives or do they have to live in the fringes. I showed the Rage Dice rules to a (non-WtA fan) buddy and he was baffled how the heck was the pc supposed to hold a job and still deal with Rage?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So I think the idea here is that there are two purposes to the Rage track: One at Rage 2+ it's an impediment to non-violent actions. Two it's a battery for werewolf powers (shifting, regeneration, gifts, rites). And so the game loop is supposed to be doing non-violent stuff while Rage is accumulated and at some point you're supposed to do something violent and while you're doing that the Rage goes back down again as powersareused. But I don't think every session can fit neatly into that loop (and havea 50/50 chance of lowering Rage, so that also can become an issue. And that's when you get these gifts and rites that lower or raise Rage.<br /> <br /> I think that's where the issue here is. The system is set up with the presumption of pushing players into violent scenarios. And the punishment of high Rage/Brutal Outcomes feels like the game telling players they're doing something wrong for not being in a violent scenario where the Rage drain is supposed to occur. And that's where the sidebar comes in to chide those players who seek to use Rage checks outside those violent scenarios because then the threat of high Rage + Brutal Outcomes can't push players into violent scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T07:50:06-07:00","id":1516779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516772#post1516772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's where the issue here is. The system is set up with the presumption of pushing players into violent scenarios. And the punishment of high Rage/Brutal Outcomes feels like the game telling players they're doing something wrong for not being in a violent scenario where the Rage drain is supposed to occur. And that's where the sidebar comes in to chide those players who seek to use Rage checks outside those violent scenarios because then the threat of high Rage + Brutal Outcomes can't push players into violent scenarios.</div> </div> </div> </div>And YET, the fiction is telling us the very opposite. That the violence is not THAT bad and the New Garou can handle life among humanity.<br /> <br /> So either there is a mechanic there to balance it all out, or the writers are really writing past each other XD<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T08:27:05-07:00","id":1516785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516779#post1516779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And YET, the fiction is telling us the very opposite. That the violence is not THAT bad and the New Garou can handle life among humanity.<br /> <br /> So either there is a mechanic there to balance it all out, or the writers are really writing past each other XD<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there's something missing here that balances this. High Rage is bad for non-violent scenarios, going past 5 causes WP damage but you're getting a big battery for your various powers. Low Rage is bad for combat as the looming threat of losing the wolf shuts down your powers and all you're getting in return is being able to avoid the negative of Brutal Outcomes. Seeking violent solutions to problems is getting more support here than making an effort to keep your Rage down and try to go for non-violent solutions.<br /> <br /> It actually does seem like if you want your connection to humanity to be stable, voluntarily losing the wolf is a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T09:04:25-07:00","id":1516794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516757#post1516757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if you are referring to me because I made a comment in another thread where rules as written for crinos says you have to kill something each turn or check for frenzy. Do I think that squishing a bug each turn is a great interpretation of the rules? No, but gamers are notorious for finding loopholes and exploiting sloppy writing and mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. This &quot;kill bis to avoid frenzy/spend WP&quot; it's a W5 version of &quot;bucket of slugs\u200b&quot; from D&amp;D 3.0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T09:52:41-07:00","id":1516803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516785#post1516785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It actually does seem like if you want your connection to humanity to be stable, voluntarily losing the wolf is a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>And given the fluff is ALL about human contact,losing the wolf is more beneficial than keeping it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T10:09:11-07:00","id":1516804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516803#post1516803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And given the fluff is ALL about human contact,losing the wolf is more beneficial than keeping it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You could actually circumvent the entire Rage track by voluntarily losing the wolf for the non-violent parts (just don't howl at the moon and you don't have to deal with Rage gains andBrutal Outcomes) and then when there's a violent contest about to occur, you do the Rite of Rage and give everyone Rage 1, then you shift into Crinos and voluntarily enter Frenzy. Only tricky bit are the two Rage checks for shifting into Crinos and you can't use Gifts. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T10:28:07-07:00","id":1516805,"title":"","content":"I do have a feeling the hauglusk and harano tracks are going to make all of this more complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T13:50:26-07:00","id":1516818,"title":"","content":"Good to see Paradox continuing the trend of telling us the right way to play their games. Who needs fun when you have developers telling us how to enjoy &quot;their &quot; game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","user":"Vendrin","date":". 07-02-2023, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T18:21:25-07:00","id":1516848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516745#post1516745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bloody hell, that's a lot of swing and misses. This reflects pretty badly on holden, I have a low opinion on Zak but he's pretty easy to bury on his own lack of merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, as stated earlier that was all stuff taken directly from statements made by the developer at the time, the reason they didn't happen is because said Developer was fire.....vigorously encouraged to leave. If that hadn't happened it was the intended trajectory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T18:28:09-07:00","id":1516849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516757#post1516757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if you are referring to me because I made a comment in another thread where rules as written for crinos says you have to kill something each turn or check for frenzy. Do I think that squishing a bug each turn is a great interpretation of the rules? No, but gamers are notorious for finding loopholes and exploiting sloppy writing and mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the sentient thing is the issue, which its not as the rules as written say nothing about Sapience or Sentience of the necessary victims, then swap out the insects for a bag of gerbils or chicks.....slightly grosser but still fits the bill.<br /> <br /> Though given that large numbers of Mockeries and Wyrmbeasts are no longer either sentient or sapient adding those qualifiers in would cause a bunch of issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T23:29:12-07:00","id":1516859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516805#post1516805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have a feeling the hauglusk and harano tracks are going to make all of this more complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Although I'm not looking forward to finding out. After all Harano and Hauglosk are two negative things you would wanna avoid. So those two would have to get in line with all the other negative things that we already know are plaguing players: Frenzy, Brutal Outcomes, losing the wolf, WP damage (from various sources)...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T23:44:35-07:00","id":1516860,"title":"","content":"It is possible that while narrative bad things, they could smooth out the impact of Rage a bit. While just things I'm making up on the spot, if Harano makes it harder to gain Rage (say, ignore 1 Rage gain per dot excluding howling at the moon per [time unit]), and Hauglosk lets you do more Rage things (like 1 free Rage Check per dot under circumstances per [time unit], but make Frenzies worse in some way), they'd still be bad things, but at lower levels the benefits would at least make the Rage Economy a bit more forgiving.<br /> <br /> I don't trust the designs much from what we've seen so far,and even the ideas I find could be interesting when taken as a whole feel inelegant compared to other designs out there, but it remains a potential place for alleviating some of the oddities in the previews so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T00:22:14-07:00","id":1516861,"title":"","content":"What makes the Rage track so much trickier than the Hunger mechanic in V5 is that there the idea is simple: The less Hunger the better, increase bad, decrease good. And so other mechanics can orient themselves around that formula. With Rage there are negatives awaiting players at both ends and depending on the situation, you either don't wanna be caught up in low Rage (and lose the wolf) or high Rage (Brutal Outcomes for non-violent actions and WP damage for going over 5... and there are more out-of-combat Rage gains than in-combat ones where presumably more Rage checks could decrease the Rage instead). And so any mechanic depressing Rage gain or increasing it would just end up further complicating the timing issue of where players would wanna be on the Rage track depending on the situation. Also, how much do you want players caught up in managing the Rage track or how will players react when they don't do that and for example have high Rage in a section where they don't wanna be in combat but Brutal Outcomes are making it hard not to seek violence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T00:45:55-07:00","id":1516862,"title":"","content":"What do you want me to say? Those tracks are supposed to be bad things, so of course having either or both at high levels (and they're 0-5 scaled too) would be bad . I have no idea what the devs actually did with all this. I'm just speculating that there is a potential for a bit of mitigation of that risk even if pursuing it in the end is probably going to be bad in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T01:35:12-07:00","id":1516864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516848#post1516848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, as stated earlier that was all stuff taken directly from statements made by the developer at the time, the reason they didn't happen is because said Developer was fire.....vigorously encouraged to leave. If that hadn't happened it was the intended trajectory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't suppose you have the statements? Martin said a lot of odd things and bad decisions but those don't spring to mind and my recollection of Holden isn't exactly positive. I could do with a laugh if he really did say those things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T01:49:33-07:00","id":1516866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516862#post1516862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you want me to say? Those tracks are supposed to be bad things, so of course having either or both at high levels (and they're 0-5 scaled too) would be bad . I have no idea what the devs actually did with all this. I'm just speculating that there is a potential for a bit of mitigation of that risk even if pursuing it in the end is probably going to be bad in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just meant it more as a rhetorical question. With all these negatives around, it will be interesting to see what the game thinks players should do with those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T04:48:47-07:00","id":1516880,"title":"","content":"Frankly, the biggest issue that I keep going back to is the fact that so much of the werewolf stuff punishes you and most of the non-werewolf doesn't. Last week's loresheets had a HUNTER organization be the safest option compared to the umbra one. The fluff focuses HEAVILY on human relations, to the point of desperately arguing against any wolf touchstones.<br /> <br /> Unless Harano or Haglust somehow make it impossible, currently losing the wolf seems to be the best strategy for the game. No Rage dice, no shifting issues, no umbral issues, you can focus on your goals with all your dice.<br /> <br /> Is this VERY contrary to the whole WEREWOLF point of the werewolf game? Yes. But if you set up the setting as the younger garou having jobs and social lives to the point of human touchstones, your mechanics should match that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T05:00:08-07:00","id":1516881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516880#post1516880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. But if you set up the setting as the younger garou having jobs and social lives to the point of human touchstones, your mechanics should match that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know<br /> I mean the &quot;come, play a Werewolf game, where the last thing you want to be a werewolf&quot; sounds a bit... strange?<br /> Younger garou having jobs and social lives is find and all, but they are Werewolf (sorry, I can't call this a Garou, too attached what that ment for decades) for... what again? To do everything to avoid to be in Crinos and stay away from the Umbra?<br /> Maybe W:tA was memed to be &quot;furry captain planet&quot; but at least you had that. <br /> W5 is... &quot;you are Werewolf for... why again? Why you are playing this game again?&quot; - feeling attached to it so far<br /> But maybe this is just me, but as far as we seen from this version, not yet managed to find anything that would and could use to lure players to try this <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T06:29:12-07:00","id":1516886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516881#post1516881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know<br /> I mean the &quot;come, play a Werewolf game, where the last thing you want to be a werewolf&quot; sounds a bit... strange?</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant was that the mechanics of W5 run contrary to the intended themes of W5. Rage should not be something that is dirt easy to trigger if a character has a very sensitive job as a safe cracker, you know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T08:01:55-07:00","id":1516891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1516864#post1516864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't suppose you have the statements? Martin said a lot of odd things and bad decisions but those don't spring to mind and my recollection of Holden isn't exactly positive. I could do with a laugh if he really did say those things.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall correctly, and its been a few years now, the G**** book and comments on the Camarilla were in his public address at the launch event ( the videos on line somewhere I'm sure). The others were a little closer to the actual release date ( not sure on the format) but they are definitely things that were said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T01:56:11-07:00","id":1516954,"title":"","content":"Friend of mine commented that w5 is too simular to v5 to justify purchase last night in the pub, low level, stripped lore street games where your having to manage your toxic dice pool and your powers arnt very good is hard to pony up for more than once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-02-2023, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T02:16:20-07:00","id":1516958,"title":"","content":"Minus whatever Harano and Hauglosk are bringing to the table, the current arrangement favors characters looking for violent solutions and afterwards having to deal with the consequences of collateral damage (due to Frenzy) and in general the difficulty of pursuing any sort of non-violent activity. But there are rewards in the system for simply pursuing a balls to the wall full-on violent approach. There's positive reinforcement in the system to do that whereas I don't see anything positive that would push characters in the opposite direction. It's just that the fluff says you should care about human connections and that violence isn't good enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T11:04:12-07:00","id":1516982,"title":"","content":"WTA really is way too front-loaded with lore for it's own good, but this is really such a vile overreaction. 'Werewolf, just like that movie'... like, nah, get fucked, what movie are you even watching? <br /> <br /> I used to get mad that The Elder Scrolls never lives up to it's own lore (which is absolutely metal by the way;<a href=\"https://youtu.be/IXF26oCxiX8?t=94\" target=\"_blank\"> the sun is a hole in the sky</a>) and that as the games go on really cool things they had either disappear (Cyrodil should be jungle, Skyrim should have sky wales and werebears, The totally-metal contemporary Nord religion got replaced by boring nine-divine worship and you can only see a few vestiges of it in the game IE you got to shor's halls but you don't know who shor is so) or just got made boring (What I assumed to be a shiva-like literal-world-eater is revealed to be a slightly more evil looking dragon, Dwarven architecture largely became more Tolkien like, Vampires living beneath frozen lakes became underworld vampires living in isolated castles , I can't say I'm happy with Falmer becoming reduced to slightly more interesting goblins, and I'd write a longer list were it more relevant) <br /> <br /> Yet people would reply &quot;well the new games are more successful&quot; <br /> My sweet summer child, <i>all </i>games are more successful nowadays. The target audience is just so much bigger, gaming is a multi-billion dollar industry now. You do not need to dumb things down to get good results. So long as it's delivered well, the mass market appreciates good worldbuilding and lore. It's why so many are happy to flock to the Witcher II/III and then pick up the books. <br /> <br /> WTA is too heavy, yeah, I think it's safe to say it's overly specific at times and it could benefit with some streamlining, but at the same time a good chunk of the fun of WTA is that you're in a religious cult with weird values and like dogs you get access to better powers through the pavlovian system of renown, which I think is arguably the cleverest thing white wolf ever did. nuWoD just doesn't have a soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T23:58:41-07:00","id":1517035,"title":"","content":"What strikes me about Rage and Rage dice is that these seem to solely exist to punish players. Were I writing a new edition of <i>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</i>, I would have introduced something like the following:<ul><li>Rage is a trait representing the primal power of werewolves, and their connection to their animalistic nature.</li> <li>Rage is gained in various contexts but, seriously, we are going to give some proper, details examples, rather than just a bit of vague guidance.</li> <li>Each point of Rage a character has provides one Rage dice. You can choose to add Rage dice to a dice pool, which represents werewolves calling upon their primal energies. Adding these dice increase the chance of success on a given roll, but also present the chance of a brutal outcome; unlike the current version of the rules, brutal outcomes are not necessarily failures, but normally present downsides.</li> <li>An example: a Glass Walker corporate spy is attempting to sneak into an office building. The character doesn't have any suitable gifts, and, for various reasons, the character is not able to use the Umbra as a shortcut. Does the character add any Rage dice to the roll? These would increase the chance of success, but also increase the chance of a brutal outcome (maybe the character would lose patience trying to pick the lock, and just batter the door down instead).</li> <li>So, players have meaningful choices; do I draw on my Rage to increase the chance of success on a given roll, but with the chance of a brutal outcome?</li> <li>We want some guidance to brutal outcomes, beyond vague hand-waving, and brutal outcomes when rolls are successes can be as interesting as when they are failures. Remember the classic werewolf trope of victims being killed in a way to suggest that they have been attacked by a wolf or monster? That's going to happen if you defeat an enemy with a brutal outcome. It may of course, be worth it.</li> <li>And then sometimes a brutal outcome won't matter at all; trying to defeat a nexus crawler? Throw all the Rage dice you have at it, you're going to need it, and there won't be any consequences for ripping off a tentacle or two with your teeth.</li> <li>If we want to have penalties for having Rage which is too high, have a mechanic forcing Rage dice into a dice pool for every point by which Rage exceeds Willpower. They are still bonus dice, mind.</li> <li>And taking actions to reduce Rage are perfectly legitimate; we don't want sidebars telling players they shouldn't take actions just to reduce Rage. There's nothing wrong with characters being aware of their Rage, and taking actions to moderate it.</li> </ul><br /> So, the above is not significantly different from Rage as written, but with some subtle differences to make Rage dice a benefit, rather than a penalty, and giving players a bit more agency to how Rage intersects with actions of a given character.<br /> <br /> (And this is my five-minute version; with a bit of effort and playtesting, you should actually be able to arrive at some mechanics which you might want to appear in the game.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T01:17:10-07:00","id":1517039,"title":"","content":"Another weird bit in the writing is that in the section for Rage-checks it says at the end: &quot;Rage decreasing in this manner doesn't necessarily represent the Garou becoming &quot;less angry&quot; but rather models how the Rage is expressed, the pent-up energy manifesting as Gifts or a more vicious supernatural form.&quot; But that principle doesn't hold for Brutal Outcomes. There Rage isn't just &quot;pent-up energy&quot;, instead it does represent some sort of anger that calls for violence and destruction. And so a Garou with decreased Rage could be considered &quot;less angry&quot; as Brutal Outcomes are less likely to occur.<br /> <br /> But from how the mechanics work, I can absolutely see a game that reflects the description from the H5-corebook: &quot;Werewolves rampage against the structures that have elevated humanity from the poverty of the past, devoting themselves to a furious primitivism enforced by fang and claw.\u200b&quot; After all, Rage becomes much less of a headache and even beneficial when you embrace violence. Like, any Brutal Outcome when you try to damage or harm something or somebody means that two or more 1s or 2s are translated into four automatic successes. You have that and combine that with the physical dice-bonuses of the Glabro/Crinos/Hispo and you're gonna win any combat-encounter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T01:35:57-07:00","id":1517040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517039#post1517039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Rage decreasing in this manner doesn't necessarily represent the Garou becoming &quot;less angry&quot; but rather models how the Rage is expressed, the pent-up energy manifesting as Gifts or a more vicious supernatural form.&quot; <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They really needed another editor for this book. This is supposed to be a newbie friendly edition and they're really over thinking the angry bar.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T01:42:04-07:00","id":1517041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517039#post1517039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all, Rage becomes much less of a headache and even beneficial when you embrace violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps<br /> IF you are a lone wolf - excuse the pun<br /> But when a pack of werewolf are in combat and are affected with anger that calls for violence and destruction (*cough* Wyrm *cough*) what will prevent them to tear <i>each other</i> in to pieces (even without runing out of enemies, maybe)? <br /> Especially with these conditions and Rage-dice?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T02:10:17-07:00","id":1517043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517040#post1517040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They really needed another editor for this book. This is supposed to be a newbie friendly edition and they're really over thinking the angry bar.</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels like conceptually they tried to both imitate the Hunger/Rouse-check-mechanic from V5 and find a way to combine Gnosis and Rage into one track. It certainly feels a bit underdeveloped, like why is the &quot;Spending Or Losing Rage&quot;- section without any narrative-first activities that correspond to Rage-loss in the same way there are activities characters can pursue to gain Rage...? You could've just brought back in &quot;Gaining Gnosis&quot;-activities from W20 like meditation or sacred hunt.<br /> <br /> It would even help if Touchstones were more relevant here (which would fit the W5 fluff more as well) but you can use the Touchstone-effect only once per story to reduce your Rage to 1. This is also btw another one of those instances that also were a problem in H5 where the book fails to cross-reference mechanics. Using your Touchstone should be listed under &quot;Spending or Losing Rage&quot; but oh well, at least they're consistent...\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517041#post1517041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps<br /> IF you are a lone wolf - excuse the pun<br /> But when a pack of werewolf are in combat and are affected with anger that calls for violence and destruction (*cough* Wyrm *cough*) what will prevent them to tear <i>each other</i> in to pieces (even without runing out of enemies, maybe)?<br /> Especially with these conditions and Rage-dice?</div> </div> </div> </div>You bank your WP and when you have to choose between spending WP or entering Frenzy in Crinos, for example, you always choose the latter. Because Frenzy is a two-step-process, first you go after what triggered Frenzy, then after dealing with that, you roll whether you will go after everything in sight. That's where you need your WP-track undamaged. But at least with this approach, Brutal Outcomes are a positive factor instead and you got your huge battery for shifting, regenerating and (before you enter Frenzy) Gifts. If you don't do that, you're not getting these advantages or have a lack of resources to use for shifting, regenerating etc. and Brutal Outcome turns into a hurdle instead. And Frenzy can still happen regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T02:23:01-07:00","id":1517045,"title":"","content":"Feels like outright stealing Satiety from <b>Beast</b> would've been super. (High Rage; good at dishing out and taking violence, bad at communal and spiritual stuff. Low Rage; vice-versa)<br /> <br /> Or stealing Inspiration from <b>Trinity Continuum</b>, but adding negative and involuntary elements. (Can do Dramatic Editing, but only towards violent ends; regaining Rage by being harmed or offended is the easiest method recharging, etc)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T03:10:01-07:00","id":1517047,"title":"","content":"Honestly, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar317_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"317\" data-vbnamecard=\"317\">James_Willoughby</a>'s house rule example really made me realise something; Why IS the Rage put onto the character all at once? While I understand the point about it being distracting, one of the things with the garou is that Rage can be channelled like a scalpel and used when needed. Clumsy and careless garou dump it all at once. But Rage Dice treat the whole thing as all or nothing, you cannot choose to use only one Rage Die to help you, they completely take over your regular dice.<br /> <br /> Which means that any garou with even 1 Rage Dice can just randomly smash what they are working on. For GWs, it means that they better not have any phones or laptops nearby since every hacking roll with Rage 2 might result in it being torn asunder and the precious willpower they need gets cut SEVERLY next session. Red Talons might have an easier time with technology than GWs, ironically.<br /> <br /> And yes, it is amazing how punishing all these supposed 'powers' are. These are things that are supposed to HELP you, yet the umbra hurts you, crinos is uncontrollable, Rage makes the (stated by the fluff) regular life hard.<br /> <br /> In older editions, the trap of Rage was how useful it was. It could save your character from death! Extra combat actions! Intimidation is easier! But too much Rage and you become basically unable to exist in the very little amount of human/wolf life you have. Heck, other GAROU start to see you as a loose cannon. Nevermind ANY Frenzy roll. Rage was like candy, delicious until you ate too much. The most important part of this was, that it was the player's own actions that often caused this trap to spring.<br /> <br /> But Rage Dice is not allowing the player to hang themselves with their actions, instead it places the noose on their neck from the outset. Which then means the Rage is treated with kid gloves all the time, which kills the whole point of it.<br /> <br /> Maybe the 5th editions are meant to just be mostly diceless or they are trying to match the movie werewolf style. Either way, if you make something that is supposed to be a strength of the character unpleasant to use? Then it will not get used because most players will hedge their bets in safer things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T03:34:51-07:00","id":1517049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517043#post1517043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels like conceptually they tried to both imitate the Hunger/Rouse-check-mechanic from V5 and find a way to combine Gnosis and Rage into one track. It certainly feels a bit underdeveloped, like why is the &quot;Spending Or Losing Rage&quot;- section without any narrative-first activities that correspond to Rage-loss in the same way there are activities characters can pursue to gain Rage...? You could've just brought back in &quot;Gaining Gnosis&quot;-activities from W20 like meditation or sacred hunt.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah it seems to be running into the issue they had with v5 disciplines with the removal of stuff requires remaining mechanics to carry more than they should-this isn't actually newbie friendly since it cognitive theory says large blocks of info should be broken up and compartilised for new learners. They're also way too invested in mechanically enforcing werewolf Rage in a way which appears potentially detrimental to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T04:31:32-07:00","id":1517053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517047#post1517047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why IS the Rage put onto the character all at once? While I understand the point about it being distracting, one of the things with the garou is that Rage can be channelled like a scalpel and used when needed. Clumsy and careless garou dump it all at once. But Rage Dice treat the whole thing as all or nothing, you cannot choose to use only one Rage Die to help you, they completely take over your regular dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Brutal Outcome is such an overly blunt thing as a game-mechanic, I feel like. Even compared to V5 because there you have Messy Criticals and Bestial Failure:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A critical win in which one or more 10s appears on a Hunger die is a messy critical. The character succeeds as in a regular critical \u2013 but like an animal would, not a being capable of foresight or self-control. The Beast scored the critical, perhaps, not you.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Okay, so there's two conditions: You need to roll a critical success <i>and </i>there needs to be one or more 10s on a Hunger-Die.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A failed roll (not enough successes to reach the Difficulty or to beat an opposing contestant\u2019s number of successes) in which one or more Hunger dice come up a 1 is a bestial failure.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Again, two conditions: You failed the roll <i>and </i>one or more Hunger-Dice have a 1.<br /> <br /> But W5 took this as inspiration and Brutal Outcome is this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On its own, a Brutal result (1s and 2s) is treated as a failure, but two or more on a single test yields a Brutal Outcome. A Brutal Outcome causes a test to fail (usually with something being wrecked, harmed or destroyed) unless the aim of the test was to cause damage or injury, in which case a Brutal Outcome yields four automatic successes. </div> </div> </div>First, &quot;Unless the aim was to cause damage or injury&quot; covers a huge spectrum of rolls you normally make in a session, I think. That plus how here you just need two or more Rage-Dice with 1s or 2s to trigger things... it doesn't even matter what you actually rolled (unlike in V5).<br /> <br /> It's like somebody looked at Hunger-Dice, Messy Criticals and Bestial Failure and thought: How can we make this mechanic more intrusive...? Also, with V5 you get multiple different examples of what to do with Messy Criticals and Bestial Failure. With Brutal Outcomes it's just &quot;Your roll fails and your character wrecks/destroys shit&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517047#post1517047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which means that any garou with even 1 Rage Dice can just randomly smash what they are working on. For GWs, it means that they better not have any phones or laptops nearby since every hacking roll with Rage 2 might result in it being torn asunder and the precious willpower they need gets cut SEVERLY next session. Red Talons might have an easier time with technology than GWs, ironically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically you can't get a Brutal Outcome with Rage 1, so there's that... but don't worry, there's still punishment awaiting the PC because if you have need of any ability (like a Gift or shifting into Glabro/Crinos/Hispo or regenerating health), a Rage-check can push you back to Rage 0 which then triggers &quot;losing the wolf&quot;. With &quot;losing the wolf&quot;, I think there you could also get an easy fix by just looking at W20 as there &quot;losing the wolf&quot; occurs when you have depleted all your Rage <i>and </i>WP-points. Same could be done here. &quot;Losing the wolf&quot; only happens when both your Rage and your WP are at 0. And just having Rage 0 means you can easily go back to Rage 1 through normal means without having to wait till night and do the whole &quot;howling at the moon&quot;-bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517047#post1517047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Rage Dice is not allowing the player to hang themselves with their actions, instead it places the noose on their neck from the outset. Which then means the Rage is treated with kid gloves all the time, which kills the whole point of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fluff is all about how bad the Get of Fenris are for embracing Rage but Brutal Outcomes is written with the idea of &quot;You either act out the Rage voluntarily - or the dice make you do it.&quot; The former gets you automatic successes, the latter makes you a failure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517047#post1517047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the 5th editions are meant to just be mostly diceless or they are trying to match the movie werewolf style. Either way, if you make something that is supposed to be a strength of the character unpleasant to use? Then it will not get used because most players will hedge their bets in safer things.</div> </div> </div> </div>With H5 there certainly was more of an emphasis on the idea of &quot;rolling dice is optional&quot;. There was that difference between V5 and H5 in its approach to &quot;Automatic Wins&quot;. In V5 the text said:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a character\u2019s dice pool is twice the task\u2019s Difficulty, the Storyteller may opt to rule that the character wins automatically without a dice roll.Automatic wins streamline play and reduce distracting rules interludes. <b>Apply them vigorously</b>, especially outside of combat or for tests where character failure is boring: information-gathering tests, conversation-openers, or gambits that open up the scene or let it move forward dramatically.\u200b\u200b </div> </div> </div> (Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> In H5 the text slightly changed:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a character\u2019s dice pool is twice the task\u2019s Difficulty, the Storyteller may opt to rule that the character wins automatically without a dice roll. Automatic wins streamline play and reduce distracting rules interludes.<br /> <br /> <b>Apply automatic wins as much as possible</b>, especially outside of combat or for tests where character failure creates no interesting outcome: information-gathering tests, conversation-openers, or gambits that open up the scene or let it move forward dramatically.\u200b </div> </div> </div> (Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> And Renegade put out aids for playing H5. This is how dealing with dice-rolls is depicted there: <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"393\" height=\"553\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/OjKgGvI.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/OjKgGvI.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/OjKgGvI.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> I assume the same attitude holds true for W5. I guess that could be why the punishing elements of the Rage-track were considered less of a problem by the developers when the assumption is that any dice-pool twice as big as the difficulty is never rolled and just assumed to be a success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T04:45:40-07:00","id":1517054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517053#post1517053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Brutal Outcome is such an overly blunt thing as a game-mechanic, I feel like. Even compared to V5 because there you have Messy Criticals and Bestial Failure:<br /> <br /> Okay, so there's two conditions: You need to roll a critical success <i>and </i>there needs to be one or more 10s on a Hunger-Die.<br /> <br /> Again, two conditions: You failed the roll <i>and </i>one or more Hunger-Dice have a 1.<br /> <br /> But W5 took this as inspiration and Brutal Outcome is this:<br /> <br /> First, &quot;Unless the aim was to cause damage or injury&quot; covers a huge spectrum of rolls you normally make in a session, I think. That plus how here you just need two or more Rage-Dice with 1s or 2s to trigger things... it doesn't even matter what you actually rolled (unlike in V5).<br /> <br /> It's like somebody looked at Hunger-Dice, Messy Criticals and Bestial Failure and thought: How can we make this mechanic more intrusive...? Also, with V5 you get multiple different examples of what to do with Messy Criticals and Bestial Failure. With Brutal Outcomes it's just &quot;Your roll fails and your character wrecks/destroys shit&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Technically you can't get a Brutal Outcome with Rage 1, so there's that... but don't worry, there's still punishment awaiting the PC because if you have need of any ability (like a Gift or shifting into Glabro/Crinos/Hispo or regenerating health), a Rage-check can push you back to Rage 0 which then triggers &quot;losing the wolf&quot;. With &quot;losing the wolf&quot;, I think there you could also get an easy fix by just looking at W20 as there &quot;losing the wolf&quot; occurs when you have depleted all your Rage <i>and </i>WP-points. Same could be done here. &quot;Losing the wolf&quot; only happens when both your Rage and your WP are at 0. And just having Rage 0 means you can easily go back to Rage 1 through normal means without having to wait till night and do the whole &quot;howling at the moon&quot;-bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> The fluff is all about how bad the Get of Fenris are for embracing Rage but Brutal Outcomes is written with the idea of &quot;You either act out the Rage voluntarily - or the dice make you do it.&quot; The former gets you automatic successes, the latter makes you a failure.<br /> <br /> <br /> With H5 there certainly was more of an emphasis on the idea of &quot;rolling dice is optional&quot;. There was that difference between V5 and H5 in its approach to &quot;Automatic Wins&quot;. In V5 the text said:<br /> (Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> In H5 the text slightly changed:<br /> (Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> And Renegade put out aids for playing H5. This is how dealing with dice-rolls is depicted there: <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"393\" height=\"553\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/OjKgGvI.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/OjKgGvI.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/OjKgGvI.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> I assume the same attitude holds true for W5. I guess that could be why the punishing elements of the Rage-track were considered less of a problem by the developers when the assumption is that any dice-pool twice as big as the difficulty is never rolled and just assumed to be a success.</div> </div> </div> </div>The flowchart is wrong. The third one need &quot;yes&quot; to remove the roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T05:19:44-07:00","id":1517055,"title":"","content":"Its probably clunky wording but Wouldn't the rage and hunger dice circumvent the third one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T06:10:51-07:00","id":1517058,"title":"","content":"How is there supposed to be a masquerade/veil if vampires/werewolves are so ridiculously out of control?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T06:21:30-07:00","id":1517059,"title":"","content":"Yeah<br /> Not that the SI is out to hunt or anything... <br /> But I guess if no survivors thanks to the Frenzy or Rage? Its... okaaaay?<br /> <br /> /sarcasm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T07:18:39-07:00","id":1517063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517059#post1517059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah<br /> Not that the SI is out to hunt or anything...<br /> But I guess if no survivors thanks to the Frenzy or Rage? Its... okaaaay?<br /> <br /> /sarcasm</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry, you have a pack member in Project Twilight to cover your tracks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T07:34:31-07:00","id":1517064,"title":"","content":"It is extremely ironic that people saying Get of Fenris was right to leave the Garou Nation after seeing the first previews are proven more and more true.<br /> <br /> I feel like the only Tribe that will feel somewhat like Werewolf will be Get of Fenris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T08:27:22-07:00","id":1517066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517059#post1517059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah<br /> Not that the SI is out to hunt or anything...<br /> But I guess if no survivors thanks to the Frenzy or Rage? Its... okaaaay?<br /> <br /> /sarcasm</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires in V5 are dysfunctional to the point that an inquisition is the least of their problems, they should flat-out be exposed to the masses. <br /> <br /> The SI is ridiculous for it's own reasons: How the fuck do you manage a secret yet globe spanning multi-agency conspiracy to violently take down a largely disconnected secret super-powered conspiracy AND keep your war secret? You can't. The logistics of such an operation are fucking impossible especially given how capable vampires are of magical spying and turning people traitor (often without them realizing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T08:38:36-07:00","id":1517070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517054#post1517054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The flowchart is wrong. The third one need &quot;yes&quot; to remove the roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they fumbled the wording there...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517055#post1517055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its probably clunky wording but Wouldn't the rage and hunger dice circumvent the third one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it kinda undermines the point of Hunger and Rage Dice... but the case in H5 is even worse actually... The special dice in H5 are Desperation-dice which is this group-based Track of 0 to 5. Each Creed gives you a Creed-Field for when you can use these Desperation-dice (like Intellectual can use it for investigation, Martial for physical conflicts etc.). But you add the Desperation-dice to your dice-pool. Now something that is never talked about in H5 is how this affects the whole Automatic Success thing. If you add three to five dice to your dice-pool, there are quite a few situations where you then end up with a dice-pool twice as big as the difficulty which... would change the dynamic of the game somewhat (to say the least).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517064#post1517064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is extremely ironic that people saying Get of Fenris was right to leave the Garou Nation after seeing the first previews are proven more and more true.<br /> <br /> I feel like the only Tribe that will feel somewhat like Werewolf will be Get of Fenris.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's weird they're portraying Get as this &quot;lost Tribe&quot; that has embraced Rage way too much... but with the rules being the way they are your PC-Garou seem pretty lost to Rage as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T14:27:21-07:00","id":1517101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517066#post1517066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires in V5 are dysfunctional to the point that an inquisition is the least of their problems, they should flat-out be exposed to the masses.<br /> <br /> The SI is ridiculous for it's own reasons: How the fuck do you manage a secret yet globe spanning multi-agency conspiracy to violently take down a largely disconnected secret super-powered conspiracy AND keep your war secret? You can't. The logistics of such an operation are fucking impossible especially given how capable vampires are of magical spying and turning people traitor (often without them realizing)</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to give you a like but it says<br /> <br /> <img title=\"Screenshot 2023-07-03 at 23-26-47 Rage-Dice - W5 Preview - Onyx Path Forums.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1284_1688419633953_621\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1284\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1284\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1284&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"Screenshot 2023-07-03 at 23-26-47 Rage-Dice - W5 Preview - Onyx Path Forums.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T15:59:14-07:00","id":1517113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517066#post1517066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires in V5 are dysfunctional to the point that an inquisition is the least of their problems, they should flat-out be exposed to the masses.<br /> <br /> The SI is ridiculous for it's own reasons: How the fuck do you manage a secret yet globe spanning multi-agency conspiracy to violently take down a largely disconnected secret super-powered conspiracy AND keep your war secret? You can't. The logistics of such an operation are fucking impossible especially given how capable vampires are of magical spying and turning people traitor (often without them realizing)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's one of the advantages of them taking the Methuselah and Elders off the board, there are fewer kindred capable of doing crazy tricks, and the mind control skills up to level five depend on certain conditions they managed to circumvent, also I can imagine a kindred using SI to eliminate a rival prince. After they have connections with important people, they can attack a nest and say it was something else, it doesn't even have to be a good story, people will rationalize. Although I think it could make a good story a group of Kindred fighting a battle against the SI and then controlling it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T16:52:09-07:00","id":1517120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517113#post1517113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's one of the advantages of them taking the Methuselah and Elders off the board, there are fewer kindred capable of doing crazy tricks, and the mind control skills up to level five depend on certain conditions they managed to circumvent, also I can imagine a kindred using SI to eliminate a rival prince. After they have connections with important people, they can attack a nest and say it was something else, it doesn't even have to be a good story, people will rationalize. Although I think it could make a good story a group of Kindred fighting a battle against the SI and then controlling it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;Let's sabotage the main factions of our game so that our new pet antagonist can have a chance rather than actually makes said antagonist competent&quot; is hardly an intelligent move.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T19:03:18-07:00","id":1517128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517120#post1517120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Let's sabotage the main factions of our game so that our new pet antagonist can have a chance rather than actually makes said antagonist competent&quot; is hardly an intelligent move.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I even think you can beat a Methuselah with a good strategy, but that would be too much to suspend disbelief. Anyway I was just talking about an &quot;advantage&quot; of this new scenario, I don't think that's why they took out the older vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T22:36:45-07:00","id":1517138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517120#post1517120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Let's sabotage the main factions of our game so that our new pet antagonist can have a chance rather than actually makes said antagonist competent&quot; is hardly an intelligent move.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Then, when this new antagonist has clearly made a MASSIVE impact on the setting, let's not allow players to even try playing them. Even though they are regular humans and not Nephandi/BSDs/etc.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T00:39:59-07:00","id":1517143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517138#post1517138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Then, when this new antagonist has clearly made a MASSIVE impact on the setting, let's not allow players to even try playing them. Even though they are regular humans and not Nephandi/BSDs/etc.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And they were right to do so. After all, playing a SI hunter would not be street level wod, and you wouldn't want to have BadWrongFun(tm), right? Right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 07-04-2023, 03:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T01:05:37-07:00","id":1517144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517143#post1517143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And they were right to do so. After all, playing a SI hunter would not be street level wod, and you wouldn't want to have BadWrongFun(tm), right? Right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean I mean, they are RELIGIOUS ZEALOTS! No one wants to play THAT, right?? /s","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T01:21:36-07:00","id":1517145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517143#post1517143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And they were right to do so. After all, playing a SI hunter would not be street level wod, and you wouldn't want to have BadWrongFun(tm), right? Right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> SI is weird because they're portrayed as untouchable and somehow worse than vampires. The game seems to constantly tiptoe around the annihilation of vampires being a net positive to humanity by trying to portray them as mustache twirlers. The trouble is its a real hard sell especially in v5 were vampires are both socially and individually more unpleasant and dangerous.<br /> <br /> As a side wod has some very.... optermistic (pessimistic?)views on how effective state surveillance digital or otherwise can be.<br /> <br /> As with a lot of 5th ed stuff it's an interesting idea which is badly implemented because the lore is more about railroading than story telling, they wanted players harrased by cia black ops units and a way to wipe the board. They should have just had the second inquisition as the main conflict development in the edition and not bothered with the other metaplot changes say gehanna gets cancelled because ravnos got carpet bombed or something. How the Sabbat, independants, anarchs and carmarilla react to a resurgence in humanities resistance to them is a lot more interesting than the current setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-04-2023, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T02:09:47-07:00","id":1517148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517145#post1517145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> SI is weird because they're portrayed as untouchable and somehow worse than vampires. The game seems to constantly tiptoe around the annihilation of vampires being a net positive to humanity by trying to portray them as mustache twirlers. The trouble is its a real hard sell especially in v5 were vampires are both socially and individually more unpleasant and dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who actually owns the Society of Leopold book physically and had read through it multiple times, the way the Second Inquisition is treated is so odd. Because a huge point with SoL is that they are NOT dumb, they are NOT just zealous idiots. They make the sacrifices they make because they know just how powerful their enemy is.<br /> <br /> It is asking the question who is truly moral, the religious hunters or the undead parasites.<br /> <br /> By making SI into a non-player faction and one that constantly is treated as worse than vampires, the whole conflict is as flat as a pancake. Then you add on that SI has actually HELPED humanity to be safer and it feels like whoever wrote this plotline considered things a bit TOO much from the vampire POV.<br /> <br /> Going back to werewolf, since the new garou are not beholden to the Litany anymore, what stops them from allying with the SI to take out vampires? I mean, if they ally with Project Twilight, surely a more straightforward organization would be even better? The only reason you can't is because there is an out-of-universe block.<br /> <br /> WoD5 is trying to be the more modern and open-minded version, but so far the way antagonist factions are treated and even WHO is the antagonist in the first place all comes across as closed-minded and moralistic.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T13:20:22-07:00","id":1517169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517148#post1517148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .<br /> <br /> Going back to werewolf, since the new garou are not beholden to the Litany anymore, what stops them from allying with the SI to take out vampires? I mean, if they ally with Project Twilight, surely a more straightforward organization would be even better? The only reason you can't is because there is an out-of-universe block.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>or even, if the litany is down the toilet, what stops werewolves from allying with the vampires? Or any creatures of the wyrm? After all, once &quot;wherever it breeds&quot; is not longuer followed, nothing stops you from chaining fomori to uses as guarding dogs to at the border of the caern, or summon banes to curse ennemies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T03:54:57-07:00","id":1517210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517169#post1517169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> or even, if the litany is down the toilet, what stops werewolves from allying with the vampires? Or any creatures of the wyrm? After all, once &quot;wherever it breeds&quot; is not longuer followed, nothing stops you from chaining fomori to uses as guarding dogs to at the border of the caern, or summon banes to curse ennemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That brings to mind that one part from the Ghost Council section:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This philosophy has earned the Ghost Council a reputation as subversives among more traditional Garou \u2014 and Ghosts don\u2019t seem to care. \u201cThe ends justify the means\u201d usually comes across as a dangerous political doctrine, but for the Ghost Council, finding an answer or opportunity excuses how it\u2019s accomplished. If something comes of maintaining a relationship with a confidant \u200bfrom a fallen tribe or forging pacts with forbidden spirits, the Ghost is satisfied \u2014 and validated, in their minds.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Makes you wonder why they kicked out the Get and the Stargazers but the Ghost Council is still okay despite their &quot;ends justify the means&quot; approach to who they work with. According to this you could expect a Ghost Council member to ally with Get, BSD, Pentex and god knows what else... As long as it accomplishes the goal, it's fine...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T11:26:29-07:00","id":1517218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517210#post1517210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That brings to mind that one part from the Ghost Council section:<br /> <br /> Makes you wonder why they kicked out the Get and the Stargazers but the Ghost Council is still okay despite their &quot;ends justify the means&quot; approach to who they work with. According to this you could expect a Ghost Council member to ally with Get, BSD, Pentex and god knows what else... As long as it accomplishes the goal, it's fine...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's also weird that they gave them gimmick of the shadow lords. The uktena were always the &quot;knowledge at all cost&quot; tribe, not so much one about doing dark deeds for reasons that aren't knowledge gathering. It makes me wonder what they'll do with with the SL.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And you're right, it's weird that they put out the stargazers and gets. Since in the end with the whole &quot;using willpower to calm rage&quot; idea, thr stargazers are the beq exemples of what the devs are doing for the garou. And the gets are ironically the best defendants of gaia compared to what is described as normal W5 garou behavior<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 07-05-2023, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T14:40:54-07:00","id":1517225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517218#post1517218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also weird that they gave them gimmick of the shadow lords. The uktena were always the &quot;knowledge at all cost&quot; tribe, not so much one about doing dark deeds for reasons that aren't knowledge gathering. It makes me wonder what they'll do with with the SL.<br /> And you're right, it's weird that they put out the stargazers and gets. Since in the end with the whole &quot;using willpower to calm rage&quot; idea, thr stargazers are the beq exemples of what the devs are doing for the garou. And the gets are ironically the best defendants of gaia compared to what is described as normal W5 garou behavior\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The Stargazer-example is especially weird because their departure from the Garou Nation is heavily thedependent on old WtA-lore. And that lore is no longer relevant to W5. With the Get, I think, we're getting a remnant of the first iteration of W5 that for whatever reason is still in this version (I like that theory certainly more than JA's explanation on Twitter...). And I think Stargazers are similar to that in just being this remnant of another version. It probably won't make sense in this version but if you think of it as a mangled copy-paste from a previous very different version then I guess it can at least explain why it's written like that...<br /> <br /> Like, take that Ghost-Council-bit... This was about finding a new definition of the Elder Brother Tribe from previous WtA-editions. And so in the first iteration of W5 the Tribe was renamed to be the Ghost Council and got a new write-up. But what we got here is the second iteration where a completely different set of developers/writers copied/rewrote parts of the first iteration. That's a strange approach but then again development wasn't exactly a standard-procedure with W5...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T15:05:15-07:00","id":1517227,"title":"","content":"Thing is... the Stargazers were there in the Revised corebook, and they had a very detailed tribebook about what they are up to and what their travels meant. They were placed into a less prominent position, said most of them moved, but any that you need can be still be found and gave you everything you need to play them in the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T15:47:25-07:00","id":1517232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517225#post1517225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Stargazer-example is especially weird because their departure from the Garou Nation is heavily thedependent on old WtA-lore. And that lore is no longer relevant to W5. With the Get, I think, we're getting a remnant of the first iteration of W5 that for whatever reason is still in this version (I like that theory certainly more than JA's explanation on Twitter...). And I think Stargazers are similar to that in just being this remnant of another version. It probably won't make sense in this version but if you think of it as a mangled copy-paste from a previous very different version then I guess it can at least explain why it's written like that...<br /> <br /> Like, take that Ghost-Council-bit... This was about finding a new definition of the Elder Brother Tribe from previous WtA-editions. And so in the first iteration of W5 the Tribe was renamed to be the Ghost Council and got a new write-up. But what we got here is the second iteration where a completely different set of developers/writers copied/rewrote parts of the first iteration. That's a strange approach but then again development wasn't exactly a standard-procedure with W5...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm genuinely impressed by the sheer chaos that is parawolf. <br /> V5 books being done by now 3/4 different studios, H5 magically appearing despite being a the euquivalent of a sublevel indie ttrpg<br /> And now W5 going from studio to studio in an orgy of incoherent visions.<br /> <br /> And that's not even talking about the video games part.<br /> <br /> Isn't there anyone at paradox seeing that the whole thing is a decapitated chicken running around?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T07:25:58-07:00","id":1517273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517232#post1517232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there anyone at paradox seeing that the whole thing is a decapitated chicken running around?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure there was, once. But consider this; The people they hired to do WoD5 ended up causing controversy, and then there was some drama from then on out. With the original crew gone, I feel a lot of the cohesion disappeared, especially as W5 went from being outsourced to in-house to outsourced AGAIN. There is a HUGE gap of years between V5 and W5, because with the original plan gone with its creator, they seemed to have no idea wtf to DO with W5.<br /> <br /> W5 coming out now is to me an effort to get at least SOMETHING out.<br /> <br /> The fact that W5 so far has really not been promising and the whole art issue is just a cherry on top of this sundae.<br /> <br /> But I need to say, one HELL of a monkey's paw on us for hating BNS XD<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 07-06-2023, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T13:02:11-07:00","id":1517302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517144#post1517144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean I mean, they are RELIGIOUS ZEALOTS! No one wants to play THAT, right?? /s</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess is possible, but this could be another game to this point, I thought nonsense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T13:10:32-07:00","id":1517303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517210#post1517210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That brings to mind that one part from the Ghost Council section:<br /> <br /> Makes you wonder why they kicked out the Get and the Stargazers but the Ghost Council is still okay despite their &quot;ends justify the means&quot; approach to who they work with. According to this you could expect a Ghost Council member to ally with Get, BSD, Pentex and god knows what else... As long as it accomplishes the goal, it's fine...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Get is Obvious now the stargazers I guess it was to avoid cutural problems. The Council only broke rules I guess, and someone knows if still have BSD and Pentex in the W5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T15:01:08-07:00","id":1517312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517273#post1517273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sure there was, once. But consider this; The people they hired to do WoD5 ended up causing controversy, and then there was some drama from then on out. With the original crew gone, I feel a lot of the cohesion disappeared, especially as W5 went from being outsourced to in-house to outsourced AGAIN. There is a HUGE gap of years between V5 and W5, because with the original plan gone with its creator, they seemed to have no idea wtf to DO with W5.<br /> <br /> W5 coming out now is to me an effort to get at least SOMETHING out.<br /> <br /> The fact that W5 so far has really not been promising and the whole art issue is just a cherry on top of this sundae.<br /> <br /> But I need to say, one HELL of a monkey's paw on us for hating BNS XD</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is clearly an impressive serie of bad decisions.<br /> <br /> Dismantling the original team was a pretty big one. Undoing the very team that is doing the very laywork of one of your ip for a mere controversy.<br /> <br /> Plus, after 4 years, the whole project is still not back to real work. And this is not guessworks, I had the chance of working in ttrpg production (montecook games to be precise) and let me tell you, if you have even the least ammount of vision, you can produce books in around two years at most, even with a shitty editor.<br /> <br /> And they can't even keep a team. Remember when a studio including the gentleman gamer was formed to make W5? Does anyone knows why they took them the project?<br /> <br /> And now we end up with a W5 that look ridiculous even for previews.<br /> <br /> And the most funny in a sad way is that even for video games adaptations, which, let's be honest, was the reason for paradox buying the ip, even for that they can't help but going haywire.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Paradox seems to have studied well at the disney's school for mismanaging ip<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T13:46:54-07:00","id":1517392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517227#post1517227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is... the Stargazers were there in the Revised corebook, and they had a very detailed tribebook about what they are up to and what their travels meant. They were placed into a less prominent position, said most of them moved, but any that you need can be still be found and gave you everything you need to play them in the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>By that same logic you could question why the Get need to be non-playable Tribe. After all, it\u2019s \u201cre-imagination, not continuation\u201d. But Get are there as new \u201csecondary antagonist\u201d (similar to hunter-orgs in H5) but Stargazers\u2026? JA said in the previews last October that they\u2019re \u201cenigmatic allies\u201d but I have no idea how this is supposed to interact with \u201cmid-Apocalypse\u201d and \u201cGarou-Nation is dead\u201d. Hopefully it isn\u2019t anything from the old lore because anything Rage-related is silly (that topic has become very obvious in W5 due to how the mechanics work) and any relations to Asia shouldn\u2019t exist anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517312#post1517312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is clearly an impressive serie of bad decisions.<br /> Dismantling the original team was a pretty big one. Undoing the very team that is doing the very laywork of one of your ip for a mere controversy.<br /> Plus, after 4 years, the whole project is still not back to real work. And this is not guessworks, I had the chance of working in ttrpg production (montecook games to be precise) and let me tell you, if you have even the least ammount of vision, you can produce books in around two years at most, even with a shitty editor.<br /> And they can't even keep a team. Remember when a studio including the gentleman gamer was formed to make W5? Does anyone knows why they took them the project?<br /> And now we end up with a W5 that look ridiculous even for previews.<br /> And the most funny in a sad way is that even for video games adaptations, which, let's be honest, was the reason for paradox buying the ip, even for that they can't help but going haywire.<br /> Paradox seems to have studied well at the disney's school for mismanaging ip</div> </div> </div> </div>Originally W5 was developed in partnership with Hunters Entertainment (Kids On Bikes, Alice Is Missing) but the glimpses we got from James Sambrano were about how development on the first iteration of W5 sucked. Maybe we\u2019ll find out more in the future but from what we\u2019ve learned so far something went very, very wrong in the development of W5\u2019s first iteration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517273#post1517273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I need to say, one HELL of a monkey's paw on us for hating BNS XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, you don\u2019t want to exchange a kind of \u201cSabbat vs Camarilla civil war\u201d with some type of Garou for a version where the Garou-Nation doesn\u2019t even exist and you\u2019re just supposed to hunker down in a caern\u2026?<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T17:23:51-07:00","id":1517524,"title":"","content":"Yeah the stuff I was hearing from the origional team didn't exactly inspire. I don't think they'd have done any better except it'd be soft retcon instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T03:03:03-07:00","id":1517548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517524#post1517524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah the stuff I was hearing from the origional team didn't exactly inspire. I don't think they'd have done any better except it'd be soft retcon instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original HE team was working under some pretty heavy restraints from Paradox and from communications I've seen the treatment of the writing team from certain figures at Paradox was incredibly toxic and tone deaf......but the writers in the HE team were actual fans and players of WtA so they were doing their best under the circumstances.<br /> <br /> For the in-house writing team of the second iteration from what I know of the freelancers for many it was their first contact with WtA and the lead Development Teams opinions on WtA and its players are well known.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T03:08:19-07:00","id":1517549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517548#post1517548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The original HE team was working under some pretty heavy restraints from Paradox and from communications I've seen the treatment of the writing team from certain figures at Paradox was incredibly toxic and tone deaf......but the writers in the HE team were actual fans and players of WtA so they were doing their best under the circumstances.<br /> <br /> For the in-house writing team of the second iteration from what I know of the freelancers for many it was their first contact with WtA and the lead Development Teams opinions on WtA and its players are well known.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats plausable, its becoming increasingly likely Paradox is a lead weight on the neck of developers of 5th edition. But doing their best isn't really 'good' however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T03:36:25-07:00","id":1517550,"title":"","content":"Remember that this is the third iteration - there was the Martin/BNS vision, there was the Hunter's iteration and this is the third one. I think we know the least about the Hunter's iteration as that's the one that got no real previews. I'd relly love to hear what happened with that one and what was their vision, but I doubt we'll hear much considering how they probably don't want to mess with Paradox and/or NDA's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T04:34:39-07:00","id":1517552,"title":"","content":"At a guesstimate from v5 I think we'd see a continuation with lots of soft reboots such as a ghost Council style shift in the uktena and an overall shift in tribes as archeotype similar to clans in the Martin led reboot while maintaining some of the ideas we've seen so far like touchstones and rage dice on your general pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T04:47:49-07:00","id":1517554,"title":"","content":"There's also the matter that they took stuff from the Hunter version and put it into the version that's about to come out. Will the writers of the Hunter-version get credited? How does it impact the NDAs they signed once that stuff is put into the public via a release? And the way James Sambrano talked about it, it doesn't seem like he was contacted about the stuff they imported from the previous iteration. He only found out that his stuff was being used when he saw the Ghost Council name in the previews (since he was the one who came up with the new name during the previous iteration of W5).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T07:15:51-07:00","id":1517560,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, the Martin/BNS version would have still been better than current state of W5. Because as much as BNS version had its issues, it still kept the core of WtA.<br /> <br /> W5 currently is,uh, it needs to decide WHAT it wants to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T07:59:54-07:00","id":1517562,"title":"","content":"Also in terms of systems I'm still very curious about two things: How does Harano and Hauglosk exactly work and are those mechanics tipping things really over the edge in making the game un-fun? And the other thing is the caern-management-system. After all, that system is the reason that they didn't just turn coterie-types into pack-types. And with pack-types you could've brought in pack-patron-spirits and various modes of play for the group into the game but alas, the game expects you to hunker down in a caern instead. But hopefully, the caern-management will at least be useful for that mode of play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T08:30:11-07:00","id":1517563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517560#post1517560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest, the Martin/BNS version would have still been better than current state of W5. Because as much as BNS version had its issues, it still kept the core of WtA.<br /> <br /> W5 currently is,uh, it needs to decide WHAT it wants to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it'd have simular issues to v5 a lot of the bad habits where present under the martinverse such as junky mechanics questionable lore and underwritten books. Not bad just not living up to its potential <br /> <br /> but yeah probably better than what we're seeing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-09-2023, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T15:05:29-07:00","id":1517832,"title":"","content":"No new previews this week. We probably ain't seeing anything more til the book is out. There is a quiz that tells you what your Werewolf &quot;Persona&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> is (basic Auspice/Tribe questionnaire). Not linking to that, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T15:42:56-07:00","id":1517835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1517832#post1517832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No new previews this week. We probably ain't seeing anything more til the book is out. There is a quiz that tells you what your Werewolf &quot;Persona&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> is (basic Auspice/Tribe questionnaire). Not linking to that, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can tell the online quiz if flawed whenever someone gets a tribe other than Glass Walkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"lin