st Tongue is its own language that has nothing to do with garou tongue. You can't overlap terms when one group uses a sumerian-ish language and other uses mostly loanwords from various languages.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T06:44:41-07:00","id":1519420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only one thing is certain: Many Garou have Garou in<br /> their family lineages, whether human or wolf. Philodoxes,<br /> galliards, and theurges all have various takes on what<br /> this means, whether Gaia\u2019s original Garou in the epoch<br /> of legend have created generations-spanning lineages of<br /> their own, or whether there\u2019s more to the superstitious<br /> \u201cseventh son of a seventh son\u201d and similar observations<br /> of past eras. Whatever the case, few argue with proof<br /> of their own pasts and those of others \u2014 but at the<br /> same time, it\u2019s almost impossible to forecast who might<br /> become werewolves in the future, casting an even more<br /> tragic pall over the Garou plight.\u200b </div> </div> </div>The book is out, and since one of our biggest questions was what makes a Garou a Garou, this is what the book has to say about it. So it isn't genetics... except when it is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T06:50:24-07:00","id":1519421,"title":"","content":"Yes if you had a Garou in your family tree it is more likely that you will have others as well, but just because you were born to the family you are not carrying a Garou Gene. Also, you can be Garou even if you have had no relatives that were Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T06:56:09-07:00","id":1519422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1519421#post1519421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes if you had a Garou in your family tree it is more likely that you will have others as well, but just because you were born to the family you are not carrying a Garou Gene. Also, you can be Garou even if you have had no relatives that were Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what's different from before? You're still Garou from birth. And you always had people ending up as kin or random Garou popping up without obvious ancestry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T07:51:03-07:00","id":1519426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1519422#post1519422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what's different from before?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely Nothing.<br /> <br /> Its kinda like how Tribes now accept anyone from anywhere regardless of gender, ethnicity etc. Which ( with the minor exceptions of the BF (Cis Men), Red Talons ( Homid Garou) and Younger Brother ( First Nations North Americans) ) is exactly as it was since late 2nd/early Revised.<br /> <br /> <br /> They just made a lot of noise about removing ' breeding' then just left things exactly as they were as of Revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 08-02-2023, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T10:27:12-07:00","id":1519462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1519421#post1519421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes if you had a Garou in your family tree it is more likely that you will have others as well, but just because you were born to the family you are not carrying a Garou Gene. Also, you can be Garou even if you have had no relatives that were Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they... use the exact term &quot;Garou gene&quot; in the text? Just asking for a concrete confirmation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T10:55:15-07:00","id":1519473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1519462#post1519462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did they... use the exact term &quot;Garou gene&quot; in the text? Just asking for a concrete confirmation.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Not everyone\u2019s a werewolf. Not everyone<br /> can become a werewolf. As near as the Garou<br /> figure it, exactly who\u2019s going to emerge as Garou<br /> is already decided by the time they\u2019re born. The find -<br /> ing-out part is where it gets complicated.\u200b<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Is it genetic? Is it wholly spiritual? Is it caused by a spe-<br /> cific event? Or is it something that lies dormant, only to<br /> be awoken by a horrific event that rouses Rage and leaves<br /> the individual marked forever after? Whereas ideas like<br /> the \u201ccurse of the moon-beasts\u201d are certainly florid (and<br /> more than a bit lurid), is there something to the idea that<br /> the Garou condition is provoked rather than innate?\u200b<br /> <br /> Only one thing is certain: Many Garou have Garou in<br /> their family lineages, whether human or wolf. Philodox-<br /> es, galliards, and theurges all have various takes on what<br /> this means, whether Gaia\u2019s original Garou in the epoch<br /> of legend have created generations-spanning lineages of<br /> their own, or whether there\u2019s more to the superstitious<br /> \u201cseventh son of a seventh son\u201d and similar observations<br /> of past eras. Whatever the case, few argue with proof<br /> of their own pasts and those of others \u2014 but at the<br /> same time, it\u2019s almost impossible to forecast who might<br /> become werewolves in the future, casting an even more<br /> tragic pall over the Garou plight.\u200b<br /> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T11:14:26-07:00","id":1519480,"title":"","content":"What I understand is that Garou are commonly born to someone from another Garou's bloodline, but it can also spawn in any random unrelated, makes sense I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T11:14:29-07:00","id":1519481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1519462#post1519462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did they... use the exact term &quot;Garou gene&quot; in the text? Just asking for a concrete confirmation.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they say that they don't know why someone becomes Garou, but they do say that most Garou do have a Garou ancestor somewhere in their lineage.<br /> <br /> The main difference is primarily semantic except that you do not have to somehow justify that you are Kinfolk and come from a line of Garou. In previous editions you had to have a connect to the Garou which in theory would mean that your family were Kinfolk on your mothers or fathers side. so you couldn't just be Garou with absolutely zero connection to the Garou your mother or father had to have the gene or be kinfolk. Now it you can just be regardless of any familial ties. You don't have to maintain breeding stock or keep the wolf populations in mind when you create your character for the most part you can just be Garou.<br /> <br /> before the only way you became Garou was through family even if they didn't know they had the gene or even if the last Garou ancestor was 100 generations removed. you had to have had that connection, now you don't.<br /> <br /> all in all it is a semantic change when it comes down to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T12:05:26-07:00","id":1519489,"title":"","content":"By the time W20 was out, Garou could also learn one of the Apis Gifts for bestowing new changer ancestry on someone, and just make it so that their kid could be kin or Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T17:43:18-07:00","id":1519537,"title":"","content":"My interest in this W5 stuff reached new lows today, but out of sheer curiousity I have a question:<br /> <br /> Delirium is still a thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T19:26:24-07:00","id":1519550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1516465-rage-dice-w5-preview?p=1519481#post1519481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No they say that they don't know why someone becomes Garou, but they do say that most Garou do have a Garou ancestor somewhere in their lineage.<br /> <br /> The main difference is primarily semantic except that you do not have to somehow justify that you are Kinfolk and come from a line of Garou. In previous editions you had to have a connect to the Garou which in theory would mean that your family were Kinfolk on your mothers or fathers side. so you couldn't just be Garou with absolutely zero connection to the Garou your mother or father had to have the gene or be kinfolk. Now it you can just be regardless of any familial ties. You don't have to maintain breeding stock or keep the wolf populations in mind when you create your character for the most part you can just be Garou.<br /> <br /> before the only way you became Garou was through family even if they didn't know they had the gene or even if the last Garou ancestor was 100 generations removed. you had to have had that connection, now you don't.<br /> <br /> all in all it is a semantic change when it comes down to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh, Lost Cubs existed in previous editions. Orphans, adopted kids, or people who just had a genetic throwback, and grew up normally and then suddenly found out they were a werewolf. Those stories existed as options for players who wanted that, but in W5 that's now the only option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg"